b-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opencloud-eu/web/commit/4aec16d75f46634d2151d12ead8cd71588ab8c88","node_id":"C_kwDONoZ2fdoAKDRhZWMxNmQ3NWY0NjYzNGQyMTUxZDEyZWFkOGNkNzE1ODhhYjhjODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opencloud-eu/web/commit/4b6a4c080c2399a631ccf09bae79146d2d7eb2d8","sha":"4b6a4c080c2399a631ccf09bae79146d2d7eb2d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencloud-eu/web/commits/4b6a4c080c2399a631ccf09bae79146d2d7eb2d8"}],"sha":"4aec16d75f46634d2151d12ead8cd71588ab8c88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencloud-eu/web/commits/4aec16d75f46634d2151d12ead8cd71588ab8c88"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/448487?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dschmidt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dschmidt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dschmidt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dschmidt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dschmidt","id":448487,"login":"dschmidt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODQ4Nw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dschmidt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dschmidt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dschmidt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dschmidt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dschmidt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dschmidt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencloud-eu/web/commits/4b6a4c080c2399a631ccf09bae79146d2d7eb2d8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T09:46:59Z","email":"dev@dominik-schmidt.de","name":"Dominik Schmidt"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T09:46:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: support image icons for apps and extensions (#3580)\n\n* feat(design-system): support image icons in OcIcon\n\nOcIcon accepts an icon next to an icon name. A named icon carries\nname, fill type and color, an image icon carries a source and an\noptional dark source and is rendered as an image. The runtime provides\nthe dark state of the current theme.\n\n* feat(design-system): support image icons in OcApplicationIcon\n\nAn image icon fills the tile. With a primary color it is displayed in\nicon size on the colored tile instead.\n\n* feat: accept image icons in app and extension declarations\n\nApps and extensions can declare their icons as named icon or image\nicon next to the plain icon name. A string is always the name of an\nicon. The sibling fill type and color fields are deprecated in favor\nof the named icon. The file type icon mapping passes image icons on,\nand the icon url of app provider apps is declared as image icon\ninstead of being detected when rendering the action.\n\n* docs(design-system): document named icons and image icons\n\n* feat: accept image icons in the remaining icon props\n\nThe components that only pass an icon on to OcIcon accept named icons\nand image icons as well: OcAvatarItem, OcSection, OcSearchBar,\nOcFileInput, the items of OcFloatingActionButton and OcBreadcrumb,\nPlainCard and NoContentMessage. Their sibling fill type and color\nprops are deprecated in favor of the named icon.\n\n* refactor: resolve dark icon variants by icon name in OcIcon\n\nWhether an icon ships a dark variant is a property of the icon set and\nnot of the place that declares the icon. OcIcon looks it up by name,\nso the file type icon mapping holds plain icons and no longer needs a\ntype of its own. ResourceIcon, the mail attachment item and the upload\nbutton no longer resolve the dark variant themselves.\n\n* refactor: merge deprecated icon fields into the icon when registering apps\n\nThe apps store merges the deprecated iconFillType and iconColor of an\napp and its file extensions into their icon once. The apps list in the\nadmin settings, the \"Open with\" actions and the file type icon mapping\nonly read the icon and no longer pass the deprecated fields on.\n\nThe deprecated fields now apply wherever the icon is shown, like the\nfields of a named icon do.\n\n* refactor: declare the fill type of host icons in the icon\n\nThe sidebar panels, actions and file extensions of the host no longer\nuse the deprecated iconFillType field. The fill type of the vault lock\nactions was the default and is dropped.\n\n* fix: apply the deprecated fill type of an app to the icons of its file extensions\n\nA file extension with an icon of its own and no fill type fell back to\nthe deprecated iconFillType of its app in the \"Open with\" actions. The\napps store merges that fallback into the icon as well.\n\n* refactor: clarify the app color fallback of file type icons\n\n* revert: apply the deprecated fill type of an app to the icons of its file extensions\n\nA fill type belongs to the icon it was declared with. The deprecated\niconFillType of an app applies to the icon of the app and is inherited\ntogether with it, but is not mixed into an icon that a file extension\ndeclares itself.\n\nThis reverts commit d3ef5007a3.\n\n* refactor: apply deprecated icon fields only to the icon they are declared with\n\nThe deprecated iconFillType and iconColor of a file extension are only\nmerged into an icon that the file extension declares itself. A file\nextension without an icon inherits the icon of its app as is.\n\n* fix: ignore file extensions of apps that are not registered\n\nRegistering a file extension for an unknown app made the file type icon\nmapping and the \"Open with\" actions fail when they looked up the app.\n\n* fix: keep the active state of sidebar nav icons that declare a fill type\n\nThe sidebar nav shows the active item with a filled icon. A named icon\nwith a fill type of its own took precedence and stopped following the\nactive state, so the nav item sets the fill type on the icon itself.\n\n* fix: keep the resource icon helpers as deprecated instead of removing them\n\n* fix: resolve dark variants by icon name in the deprecated getResourceIconName","tree":{"sha":"970cdc8261538c5c5555cc698d537f087cd08d32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencloud-eu/web/git/trees/970cdc8261538c5c5555cc698d537f087cd08d32"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencloud-eu/web/git/commits/4b6a4c080c2399a631ccf09bae79146d2d7eb2d8","verification":{"payload":"tree 970cdc8261538c5c5555cc698d537f087cd08d32\nparent ab642452daffe540a441e43aad28f164efa26be8\nauthor Dominik Schmidt <dev@dominik-schmidt.de> 1791452819 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791452819 +0200\n\nfeat: support image icons for apps and extensions (#3580)\n\n* feat(design-system): support image icons in OcIcon\n\nOcIcon accepts an icon next to an icon name. A named icon carries\nname, fill type and color, an image icon carries a source and an\noptional dark source and is rendered as an image. The runtime provides\nthe dark state of the current theme.\n\n* feat(design-system): support image icons in OcApplicationIcon\n\nAn image icon fills the tile. With a primary color it is displayed in\nicon size on the colored tile instead.\n\n* feat: accept image icons in app and extension declarations\n\nApps and extensions can declare their icons as named icon or image\nicon next to the plain icon name. A string is always the name of an\nicon. The sibling fill type and color fields are deprecated in favor\nof the named icon. The file type icon mapping passes image icons on,\nand the icon url of app provider apps is declared as image icon\ninstead of being detected when rendering the action.\n\n* docs(design-system): document named icons and image icons\n\n* feat: accept image icons in the remaining icon props\n\nThe components that only pass an icon on to OcIcon accept named icons\nand image icons as well: OcAvatarItem, OcSection, OcSearchBar,\nOcFileInput, the items of OcFloatingActionButton and OcBreadcrumb,\nPlainCard and NoContentMessage. Their sibling fill type and color\nprops are deprecated in favor of the named icon.\n\n* refactor: resolve dark icon variants by icon name in OcIcon\n\nWhether an icon ships a dark variant is a property of the icon set and\nnot of the place that declares the icon. OcIcon looks it up by name,\nso the file type icon mapping holds plain icons and no longer needs a\ntype of its own. ResourceIcon, the mail attachment item and the upload\nbutton no longer resolve the dark variant themselves.\n\n* refactor: merge deprecated icon fields into the icon when registering apps\n\nThe apps store merges the deprecated iconFillType and iconColor of an\napp and its file extensions into their icon once. The apps list in the\nadmin settings, the \"Open with\" actions and the file type icon mapping\nonly read the icon and no longer pass the deprecated fields on.\n\nThe deprecated fields now apply wherever the icon is shown, like the\nfields of a named icon do.\n\n* refactor: declare the fill type of host icons in the icon\n\nThe sidebar panels, actions and file extensions of the host no longer\nuse the deprecated iconFillType field. The fill type of the vault lock\nactions was the default and is dropped.\n\n* fix: apply the deprecated fill type of an app to the icons of its file extensions\n\nA file extension with an icon of its own and no fill type fell back to\nthe deprecated iconFillType of its app in the \"Open with\" actions. The\napps store merges that fallback into the icon as well.\n\n* refactor: clarify the app color fallback of file type icons\n\n* revert: apply the deprecated fill type of an app to the icons of its file extensions\n\nA fill type belongs to the icon it was declared with. The deprecated\niconFillType of an app applies to the icon of the app and is inherited\ntogether with it, but is not mixed into an icon that a file extension\ndeclares itself.\n\nThis reverts commit d3ef5007a3.\n\n* refactor: apply deprecated icon fields only to the icon they are declared with\n\nThe deprecated iconFillType and iconColor of a file extension are only\nmerged into an icon that the file extension declares itself. A file\nextension without an icon inherits the icon of its app as is.\n\n* fix: ignore file extensions of apps that are not registered\n\nRegistering a file extension for an unknown app made the file type icon\nmapping and the \"Open with\" actions fail when they looked up the app.\n\n* fix: keep the active state of sidebar nav icons that declare a fill type\n\nThe sidebar nav shows the active item with a filled icon. A named icon\nwith a fill type of its own took precedence and stopped following the\nactive state, so the nav item sets the fill type on the icon itself.\n\n* fix: keep the resource icon helpers as deprecated instead of removing them\n\n* fix: resolve dark variants by icon name in the deprecated getResourceIconName","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx2aTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHlUQAFWrnVXSKmfrilelDYiuhXS8\nsrEb4l2I0k5q16ymZA5HmNhWPZsHOpjGJnck32hR0PB6K+bU0+mW6Z9uDQ/FiV3H\nu0mwfYrvxgFZUnQ+znHIrVH1njg5Bm2LAcPk20QGJ0YkhvRnuJFqUmgGRzQVnjze\nJf3xhqzn+jYohDv88ofGNYMnhEZa+/sncLKrW0KXn3u4DoMrTPuc7yTQcBnXeWtu\nIXXlCu1/bxybF+xAr3p469EUlzeyOdw6hqZAQGq5DlLagHUKWQtw5wUoe+yKjnMZ\nnL6oq1QeQ12A9suVNbpGwi8GdKyl5QiBFYGtikHeXzoLZnaRS8DWwy5h4cnJ33BG\nl84jIemMXftgSbIrz0Yfz6ndKmkZ+0cWXGFLBo+wxcbt+y9dDSG4+ih68FAhT4Gn\n3mMVat1V+MjKQKCB8HfTS3cW/6glbdhWst57a/j/44sFYdpJ8NbrUhQiGTBrmhc/\nHF30Ft+o7/fgbNW95BgJwRS0ahs6VRIS5/GM3z4s16yS4UGSTAtJ7Q15gGtLWNk5\nz9Fo8C8FEJL4Z4yicPxlcNigXR/4xprvOC3HuJ9u+sO99xnZiI9qPbZVwW5O8gX9\ntwa4RqOQ7BniNLblAyppQGcgYSOa21U8Z47Kaf8rjR1upf4ISUxdXIaB9O03T/DS\nS9py/c49/dxuIbDOiyCD\n=ipRX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T09:46:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.githu