api.github.com/users/magkue/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/magkue/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/magkue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/magkue/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/magkue","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/commits/f0b1c0872ea65c1b9775b6d0d82e3689efc4b159/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T07:59:20Z","email":"73171182+magkue@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Magnus Kühne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T07:59:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add ParticipantNavigation and pass the table order to onRowClick (#286)\n\n* Add ParticipantNavigation and pass the table order to onRowClick\n\nParticipantNavigation puts previous / next buttons on a participant''s detail\npage, at the left and right edge with the position centered between them.\ncolorByStatus tints them by pass status, wrapAround continues past the ends;\nboth default to off. getNavigationNeighbors is exported for pages that need\nthe neighbors without the buttons.\n\nPromptTable''s onRowClick now also receives every row as the table shows it\n(searched, filtered and sorted, across all pages), so a detail page can step\nthrough the rows in the order the user saw.\n\n* Pass the table order through CoursePhaseParticipationsTable\n\nonClickRowAction now also receives the ordered rows, so pages built on the\nshared participants table can step through participants in the order shown.\n\n* Simplify ParticipantNavigation\n\nDrop the unused wrapAround option and keep getNavigationNeighbors internal.\nIt now returns the neighboring participants instead of ids, which removes the\nlookup map. Remove the icon size classes Button already applies and fix the\nunclosed code block in the README.","tree":{"sha":"46e8f7b2c85a16f2bd47f8c0575d6081fab2c930","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/git/trees/46e8f7b2c85a16f2bd47f8c0575d6081fab2c930"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/git/commits/f0b1c0872ea65c1b9775b6d0d82e3689efc4b159","verification":{"payload":"tree 46e8f7b2c85a16f2bd47f8c0575d6081fab2c930\nparent d3a625bbffda3e920fe49e5344a8c2ec91ded853\nauthor Magnus Kühne <73171182+magkue@users.noreply.github.com> 1791187160 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791187160 +0200\n\nAdd ParticipantNavigation and pass the table order to onRowClick (#286)\n\n* Add ParticipantNavigation and pass the table order to onRowClick\n\nParticipantNavigation puts previous / next buttons on a participant''s detail\npage, at the left and right edge with the position centered between them.\ncolorByStatus tints them by pass status, wrapAround continues past the ends;\nboth default to off. getNavigationNeighbors is exported for pages that need\nthe neighbors without the buttons.\n\nPromptTable''s onRowClick now also receives every row as the table shows it\n(searched, filtered and sorted, across all pages), so a detail page can step\nthrough the rows in the order the user saw.\n\n* Pass the table order through CoursePhaseParticipationsTable\n\nonClickRowAction now also receives the ordered rows, so pages built on the\nshared participants table can step through participants in the order shown.\n\n* Simplify ParticipantNavigation\n\nDrop the unused wrapAround option and keep getNavigationNeighbors internal.\nIt now returns the neighboring participants instead of ids, which removes the\nlookup map. Remove the icon size classes Button already applies and fix the\nunclosed code block in the README.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw1jYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqBwQAFbZ0AznlaC0GohojAgqpYNQ\nZmj9cHVLRtM9WLd58IKceDLxCU8S44MqqpGl+OUyk+e8mcqVQAitDjJfX/74s71u\nZsKnJIpzqsV+Rny3FBgL7PdYDVHQom4W/Pop8P+icxGJgq4hl/Ip1RTgoTJ8DsLU\n8nvUgsj4ypHgOcZmeENhgpwsbOWh272DYNTJBV5