users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/commit/59b017481966434e6efda891f51f2279c1426a5b","node_id":"C_kwDONqH1h9oAKDU5YjAxNzQ4MTk2NjQzNGU2ZWZkYTg5MWY1MWYyMjc5YzE0MjZhNWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/commit/f73aea78bb9c8ea0dbdb9c4fc7771261d1f46845","sha":"f73aea78bb9c8ea0dbdb9c4fc7771261d1f46845","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/commits/f73aea78bb9c8ea0dbdb9c4fc7771261d1f46845"}],"sha":"59b017481966434e6efda891f51f2279c1426a5b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/commits/59b017481966434e6efda891f51f2279c1426a5b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53191688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rappm","id":53191688,"login":"rappm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTkxNjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/commits/f73aea78bb9c8ea0dbdb9c4fc7771261d1f46845/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T14:43:01Z","email":"53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maximilian Rapp"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T14:43:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Allow typing dates and add an optional time to the date pickers (#281)\n\n* Add Vitest and date input parsing helpers\n\nAdds a node-environment Vitest setup with a CI step and keeps test files\nout of the tsc build. The first tests cover the helpers the date pickers\nuse to parse and format typed dates (dd.MM.yyyy, d.M.yyyy, dd/MM/yyyy\nand ISO) and to apply an HH:mm time to a date.\n\n* DatePicker: Allow typing the date with the keyboard\n\nThe trigger button becomes a text field showing dd.MM.yyyy with a\ncalendar button inside it. Typed text commits on Enter or blur, is\nflagged with aria-invalid while it is not a real day, and reverts to the\nlast valid date when left unparseable. Clearing the field selects no\ndate. The picker also takes id, className and placeholder.\n\n* DatePicker: Add an optional time next to the date\n\nwithTime adds an HH:mm time field beside the date field. Picking or\ntyping a new date keeps the selected time, and a first date gets\ndefaultTime (00:00 unless set, e.g. 23:59 for an end date). A time typed\nbefore any date is kept and applied once a date is picked.\n\n* DatePicker: Move the typed-date handling into a reusable hook\n\nuseDateInputDraft owns the draft text, the invalid flag and the\nEnter/Escape/blur commit rules, so the range picker can drive its two\nfields the same way. Behavior is unchanged.\n\n* DatePickerWithRange: Allow typing the start and end dates\n\nThe trigger button becomes one bordered control with separate start and\nend text fields and a calendar button that opens the existing range\npopover. Each field parses and commits like DatePicker. A typed end\nbefore the start swaps them so the range stays ordered, and clearing\nboth fields selects no range.\n\nThe hardcoded id=''date'' on the old trigger is gone. The calendar button\nis reachable by its ''Open calendar'' label instead.\n\n* Document the typable date pickers and the unit tests\n\n* DatePickerWithRange: Never select an end without a start\n\nClearing the start or typing only an end selected { from: undefined,\nto }, a range the calendar never emits and that consumers building a\nfilter from `from` silently applied. Such an end now stays in the end\nfield as a pending date and selects no range until a start is typed.\n\nA start typed after the end now clears the end, as it starts a new\nrange like picking it in the calendar, instead of swapping the two. An\nend typed before the start still swaps them. The rules live in the\nunit-tested resolveTypedRange helper.\n\n* DatePicker: Name the date field and follow defaultTime changes\n\nWithout an id the date field now gets aria-label=''Date'', so it has an\naccessible name besides its placeholder. The label can be overridden,\nand with an id the field is left to its <Label htmlFor>.\n\ndefaultTime is now read on every render until a time is typed, so a\nchanged prop applies without overriding the user''s input. The className\ndoc comment says that only a width class replaces the default width.","tree":{"sha":"892d8c10d374d4b6eb8a219ad291aea17494a7c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/git/trees/892d8c10d374d4b6eb8a219ad291aea17494a7c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/git/commits/f73aea78bb9c8ea0dbdb9c4fc7771261d1f46845","verification":{"payload":"tree 892d8c10d374d4b6eb8a219ad291aea17494a7c7\nparent efb5e5076b817b6b3e79c84f6144118f604d6c60\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1790260981 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790260981 +0200\n\nAllow typing dates and add an optional time to the date pickers (#281)\n\n* Add Vitest and date input parsing helpers\n\nAdds a node-environment Vitest setup with a CI step and keeps test files\nout of the tsc build. The first tests cover the helpers the date pickers\nuse to parse and format typed dates (dd.MM.yyyy, d.M.yyyy, dd/MM/yyyy\nand ISO) and to apply an HH:mm time to a date.\n\n* DatePicker: Allow typing the date with the keyboard\n\nThe trigger button becomes a text field showing dd.MM.yyyy with a\ncalendar button inside it. Typed text commits on Enter or blur, is\nflagged with aria-invalid while it is not a real day, and reverts to the\nlast valid date when left unparseable. Clearing the field selects no\ndate. The picker also takes id, className and placeholder.\n\n* DatePicker: Add an optional time next to the date\n\nwithTime adds an HH:mm time field beside the date field. Picking or\ntyping a new date keeps the selected time, and a first date gets\ndefaultTime (00:00 unless set, e.g. 23:59 for an end date). A time typed\nbefore any date is kept and applied once a date is picked.\n\n* DatePicker: Move the typed-date handling into a reusable hook\n\nuseDateInputDraft owns the draft text, the invalid flag and the\nEnter/Escape/blur commit rules, so the range picker can drive its two\nfields the same way. Behavior is unchanged.\n\n* DatePickerWithRange: Allow typing the start and end dates\n\nThe trigger button becomes one bordered control with separate start and\nend text fields and a calendar button that opens the existing range\npopover. Each field parses and commits like DatePicker. A typed end\nbefore the start swaps them so the range stays ordered, and clearing\nboth fields selects no range.\n\nThe hardcoded id=''date'' on the old trigger is gone. The calendar button\nis reachable by its ''Open calendar'' label instead.\n\n* Document the typable date pickers and the unit tests\n\n* DatePickerWithRange: Never select an end without a start\n\nClearing the start or typing only an end selected { from: undefined,\nto }, a range the calendar never emits and that consumers building a\nfilter from `from` silently applied. Such an end now stays in the end\nfield as a pending date and selects no range until a start is typed.\n\nA start typed after the end now clears the end, as it starts a new\nrange like picking it in the calendar, instead of swapping the two. An\nend typed before the start still swaps them. The rules live in the\nunit-tested resolveTypedRange helper.\n\n* DatePicker: Name the date field and follow defaultTime changes\n\nWithout an id the date field now gets aria-label=''Date'', so it has an\naccessible name besides its placeholder. The label can be overridden,\nand with an id the field is left to its <Label htmlFor>.\n\ndefaultTime is now read on every render until a time is typed, so a\nchanged prop applies without overriding the user''s input. The className\ndoc comment says that only a width class replaces the default width.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtTb1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZ/EQAKQQx3jgEs1VrJiMVFGgdnU8\nqFl7oqxKXycxcflIjNuRmt0niTs+Lo0d721QMsZz4aIha3oSOHjsKB/WzUHeQJpX\nYudEVpowGCGsWRU2UFhrjvmf318jW3Ru484lSfCYBt7ovGLWKlMLzrHAmeic+mDT\naegjY8T5ExF8yylTTnHOUraMSdUmJ/522lQQ9LhtuAGqy14dIodN993kliAWAvz0\nPFmtPLIStjSLEPE9NKSdxfo/djU1wQBdRApqbWhVXR9Ot3iOjyUdrHRzBXYCtWF8\n7jRRkqX3BNEyCfu/WHpsDCumEpski55P+pZWuXld2U/7uY8twA06QL3CwOhLJUsF\nUf20oVBNZH58OqB6GZ2vSkqkDPxoWUweFiEzmpccRntzF/2Che0JRxQQU1SMo9Xs\n1Ubu24ANBMswnq38hvsZ3T3VZ95MuGgWMkpIB6bEde+1EoGDqF4ZjYDkAU2VmUWJ\nV2vxB4NL9IkaG3KVwTs20O+6cRWcQBzwGWUe5Nk6s0BLoqJtB8F2bkPORxnSs48+\n9D9H0ENl7yPH7UzSew2yRsYOuE/6JIuoOfpQVNfWrw0LNp6yBXuO7ppP3TaJQz79\nGTK6VI9xt8J9F1tw4eiwdweB5VMApy9HtThYIHc2lUK15ySmwtkwMCtWWgT8U863\nutpEST4emHX/YvFERg3e\n=dPMM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T14:43:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/commit/f73aea78bb9c8ea0dbdb9c4fc7771261d1f46845","node_id":"C_kwDONqH1h9oAKGY3M2FlYTc4YmI5YzhlYTBkYmRiOWM0ZmM3NzcxMjYxZDFmNDY4NDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/commit/efb5e5076b817b6b3e79c84f6144118f604d6c60","sha":"efb5e5076b817b6b3e79c84f6144118f604d6c60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/commits/efb5e5076b817b6b3e79c84f6144118f604d6c60"}],"sha":"f73aea78bb9c8ea0dbdb9c4fc7771261d1f46845","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/commits/f73aea78bb9c8ea0dbdb9c4fc7771261d1f46845"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/2740?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/renovate","id":29139614,"login":"renovate[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90MjkxMzk2MTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/r