d6766152c831373440d7a5c1b5e397edeee7","sha":"1109d6766152c831373440d7a5c1b5e397edeee7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/commits/1109d6766152c831373440d7a5c1b5e397edeee7"}],"sha":"327fb543f0c31f60982d2732ae07a0b8593fd335","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/commits/327fb543f0c31f60982d2732ae07a0b8593fd335"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53191688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rappm","id":53191688,"login":"rappm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTkxNjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/commits/1109d6766152c831373440d7a5c1b5e397edeee7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T16:26:11Z","email":"53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maximilian Rapp"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T16:26:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Show exported application answers as a sectioned list instead of a table (#275)\n\n* Sort exported application answers by the order the backend actually sends\n\nThe provided-output DTO transfers `order_num`, while the declared\n`ExportedApplicationAnswer` says `orderNum`. Sorting on the camelCase name\ncompared two undefined values, so the comparator returned NaN and the list kept\nwhatever order `jsonb_agg` happened to produce. The same DTO sends multi-select\nanswers as arrays although the type says `string`.\n\nModel both in a local runtime type, resolve the order from `order_num` with an\n`orderNum` fallback, and place records without a usable order last. The prop\ntype widens rather than narrows, so consumers passing `ExportedApplicationAnswer[]`\nkeep compiling. Sorting now works on a copy instead of mutating the caller''s array.\n\n* Show exported application answers as a sectioned list instead of a table\n\nThe Application phase moved its participant answers view from a dense table to a\nsectioned card list. The Interview phase renders the same applicant''s answers\nthrough this component and still looked like the old table, so the two views had\ndrifted apart visually.\n\nReplace the Type/Key/Answer table with the same sectioned layout: a numbered\ngutter, a type icon behind a focusable tooltip trigger, the question heading, and\nthe answer in an accented panel. Multi-select answers become badges; empty\nanswers get the dashed \"Not answered\" placeholder rather than a blank panel.\n\nAn access key is not unique and may even be whitespace only, so a blank heading\nfalls back to a generated question label. An empty list now renders nothing at\nall instead of a bare table header, which the interview page already handles with\nits own message.\n\n* Bump version to 1.5.0","tree":{"sha":"ceac89d781fd1aaaa32221ef558369376cc737b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/git/trees/ceac89d781fd1aaaa32221ef558369376cc737b6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/git/commits/1109d6766152c831373440d7a5c1b5e397edeee7","verification":{"payload":"tree ceac89d781fd1aaaa32221ef558369376cc737b6\nparent 7c7a1bf36d6b6ca51d8a7804cdc9dd37e8cc661b\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1790007971 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790007971 +0200\n\nShow exported application answers as a sectioned list instead of a table (#275)\n\n* Sort exported application answers by the order the backend actually sends\n\nThe provided-output DTO transfers `order_num`, while the declared\n`ExportedApplicationAnswer` says `orderNum`. Sorting on the camelCase name\ncompared two undefined values, so the comparator returned NaN and the list kept\nwhatever order `jsonb_agg` happened to produce. The same DTO sends multi-select\nanswers as arrays although the type says `string`.\n\nModel both in a local runtime type, resolve the order from `order_num` with an\n`orderNum` fallback, and place records without a usable order last. The prop\ntype widens rather than narrows, so consumers passing `ExportedApplicationAnswer[]`\nkeep compiling. Sorting now works on a copy instead of mutating the caller''s array.\n\n* Show exported application answers as a sectioned list instead of a table\n\nThe Application phase moved its participant answers view from a dense table to a\nsectioned card list. The Interview phase renders the same applicant''s answers\nthrough this component and still looked like the old table, so the two views had\ndrifted apart visually.\n\nReplace the Type/Key/Answer table with the same sectioned layout: a numbered\ngutter, a type icon behind a focusable tooltip trigger, the question heading, and\nthe answer in an accented panel. Multi-select answers become badges; empty\nanswers get the dashed \"Not answered\" placeholder rather than a blank panel.\n\nAn access key is not unique and may even be whitespace only, so a blank heading\nfalls back to a generated question label. An empty list now renders nothing at\nall instead of a bare table header, which the interview page already handles with\nits own message.\n\n* Bump version to 1.5.0","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsVqjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAi6gQAHLZ1mDyWMVYq6kMHuIwncdQ\nEHj2O3SvA6sfmKmROmUckREq2LICACCv6h/dwuN8WkM6/44j/m6poFxw83MQqOfK\nK9ad13n0Z8