"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53191688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rappm","id":53191688,"login":"rappm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTkxNjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/commits/bea39b1b899a00499e869156d3d05b10925e92e3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T10:50:30Z","email":"53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maximilian Rapp"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T10:50:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Let a server-paged PromptTable hand back its own search, sorting and pagination (#266)\n\nPromptTable always rendered a search box, sortable column headers and a\npagination bar, and all three act on the rows currently in `data`. That is\nright for a table holding the whole data set and wrong for one fed a single\nserver page: the search narrows the page rather than the data set, so a term\nthat matches a row on another page reads as \"0 rows\", and the headers reorder\nthe page while looking like they sorted the whole log.\n\nConsumers can now hand those concerns over with `serverDriven`, either per\nconcern or as `true` for all three:\n\n- `search` drops the search box and turns off the global filter\n  (`enableGlobalFilter: false`), and no longer seeds it from\n  `initialState.globalFilter` so no search badge can outlive the box. The\n  filter menu lives inside the search box, so when the box goes it gets its\n  own button and column filters stay reachable.\n- `sorting` sets `enableSorting: false` and `manualSorting: true`, so headers\n  render as plain text and the server''s row order survives. The exported\n  SortableHeader also renders plain text for a column that cannot sort, which\n  covers consumers that use it in a custom header.\n- `pagination` sets `manualPagination: true` and drops the pagination bar, so\n  the page arrives as it was fetched instead of being sliced again.\n\nWith no client-side filtering left to report, the info bar no longer claims\n\"No filters selected\" underneath a consumer''s own filter bar.\n\nAlso replace createChangeHandler, which read the resolved next value out of a\nReact setState updater and passed it to the external callback right after,\nbefore React was guaranteed to have run the updater; the callback could fire\nwith `undefined`. The table state setters are now handed to the table directly\nand the external callbacks fire from an effect once the new value is committed,\nwhich makes onSearchChange and onSortingChange safe to hang a server request\non. As a side effect they no longer fire when the committed value is unchanged.","tree":{"sha":"d86785fe454552110e785f5a602e8172c09cedd9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/git/trees/d86785fe454552110e785f5a602e8172c09cedd9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/git/commits/bea39b1b899a00499e869156d3d05b10925e92e3","verification":{"payload":"tree d86785fe454552110e785f5a602e8172c09cedd9\nparent d22519bb104d93de9701ec0124831dee711b6242\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1789037430 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789037430 +0100\n\nLet a server-paged PromptTable hand back its own search, sorting and pagination (#266)\n\nPromptTable always rendered a search box, sortable column headers and a\npagination bar, and all three act on the rows currently in `data`. That is\nright for a table holding the whole data set and wrong for one fed a single\nserver page: the search narrows the page rather than the data set, so a term\nthat matches a row on another page reads as \"0 rows\", and the headers reorder\nthe page while looking like they sorted the whole log.\n\nConsumers can now hand those concerns over with `serverDriven`, either per\nconcern or as `true` for all three:\n\n- `search` drops the search box and turns off the global filter\n  (`enableGlobalFilter: false`), and no longer seeds it from\n  `initialState.globalFilter` so no search badge can outlive the box. The\n  filter menu lives inside the search box, so when the box goes it gets its\n  own button and column filters stay reachable.\n- `sorting` sets `enableSorting: false` and `manualSorting: true`, so headers\n  render as plain text and the server''s row order survives. The exported\n  SortableHeader also renders plain text for a column that cannot sort, which\n  covers consumers that use it in a custom header.\n- `pagination` sets `manualPagination: true` and drops the pagination bar, so\n  the page arrives as it was fetched instead of being sliced again.\n\nWith no client-side filtering left to report, the info bar no longer claims\n\"No filters selected\" underneath a consumer''s own filter bar.\n\nAlso replace createChangeHandler, which read the resolved next value out of a\nReact setState updater and passed it to the external callback right after,\nbefore React was guaranteed to have run the updater; the callback could fire\nwith `undefined`. The table state setters are now handed to the table directly\nand the external callbacks fire from an effect once the new value is committed,\nwhich makes onSearchChange and onSortingChange safe to hang a server request\non. As a side effect they no longer fire when the committed value is unchanged.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoot2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+wYQACiRiIQt9ec8iCmJyAz35DoO\nodgnNNWcFWB/e1O8Cff1+WWifGvjjgm44+UMp3CB2jJqkNkNOtW0hYfUMHzrXiYS\nMUqZgXFGQGlRk6qf4XwxhfgZL1x/TDNDkDn+8KW6mpnOjkKMa5bGGKgD9g3Jd0GM\npvECKU+PfbOwHqDBU/mOzk1XRHJeB3iVYcRhl2MwCwrYv1nfpU028SMwIOp7SjtC\ntXT+3AvHs+SQMJjAVx4W1sBW5rUnXJSZ3thK7oC21V0+DJ9FzZutIawl3ilxmsw3\njljlBUYu9kiHxwlj77joReyHQx0uyIpMWY1+nPQhe+NJ66CRHyZhVsKW5n4KNaD+\n7/jJ4sycaxGpj3p5sWCsJ59u6Bj9pDC5zdR6CFzNMuarFwHBjWrBPterGDg1DwVx\nFeJ1mOQMQhyHQOEK+KuyUMF4+nRw3BmUWuHRyBOBu25psmw8JA5tyUh/LZ2eD1uk\nXdEXfbe6XIk7kcd+qbVimqzIt3HSN/wUpK75Kbr1iogUoH9NfB6VydfEwug4uqEV\nfx2fYeNFZE8OBziLbbxzVCwbFakhvu6K+uEQzat4jsCyQhM9i0pvIearmjc+nOij\nv8jQu3mqTOhNz8NHSanhu4xuENiO61OGcDBZLo7fLQ+/PKCNSLSk8STn5LlehP2a\nB44Dbg+MXrtRU/y+qJDh\n=K3xW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-10T10:50:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/commit/bea39b1b899a00499e869156d3d05b10925e92e3","node_id"