"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/renovate","id":29139614,"login":"renovate[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90MjkxMzk2MTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/commits/79969dde61ffa4a32e7074649f4f5137b3a77527/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T22:29:52Z","email":"29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"renovate[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T22:29:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Dependencies: Update all non-major dependencies (#261)\n\n* Dependencies: Update all non-major dependencies\n\n* Align @tiptap/core with the other tiptap packages\n\nRenovate left @tiptap/core at 3.30.2 while bumping every other tiptap\npackage to 3.31.0. Because tiptap exact-pins @tiptap/core as a peer\nacross its own packages, this pulled a second nested copy of\n@tiptap/core under @tiptap/starter-kit, so the extension commands\n(toggleBold, toggleBulletList, setParagraph, ...) were typed against a\ndifferent core than the one the editor imports and the build failed.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Maximilian Rapp <maximilian.rapp@tum.de>","tree":{"sha":"ecf01fd0698abf3f456711d381841512f677c4ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/git/trees/ecf01fd0698abf3f456711d381841512f677c4ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/git/commits/79969dde61ffa4a32e7074649f4f5137b3a77527","verification":{"payload":"tree ecf01fd0698abf3f456711d381841512f677c4ae\nparent 04af868fc40be836391858b546587c61646bb996\nauthor renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1788906592 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788906592 +0100\n\nDependencies: Update all non-major dependencies (#261)\n\n* Dependencies: Update all non-major dependencies\n\n* Align @tiptap/core with the other tiptap packages\n\nRenovate left @tiptap/core at 3.30.2 while bumping every other tiptap\npackage to 3.31.0. Because tiptap exact-pins @tiptap/core as a peer\nacross its own packages, this pulled a second nested copy of\n@tiptap/core under @tiptap/starter-kit, so the extension commands\n(toggleBold, toggleBulletList, setParagraph, ...) were typed against a\ndifferent core than the one the editor imports and the build failed.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Maximilian Rapp <maximilian.rapp@tum.de>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoIxgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAavgQAHCwahHME1vzITDQnPLVdkPb\nVsjYDQFnsjCXdH4ddvT9PBbrwD2jJcd+wK9PRPa/EM53uJ3jPMs8mFOVLJC7Ew0D\nql6RFpqfkVxQzx9mQHbjoqCKfWZrqMRkn9OkGnXyfhGW/d6pvIOWphRBIE9D6Di7\nyyZICxmkRQRbUnSM+iWQBUfBSC0iuhQfjhxkNvbcCZKniIbFFatQ/Ppo1hUfsz0o\nQOPy4bUxA+zQLV5OlPk3mPL0O1IPLYtGAjeP+EhVel4gvLZwyXPziDaVHK1rVZ1s\nxYIl9E34F9dccumSovNmZKCyhAme9uQJb6gupJPG6YJKKXHam9qqQLKiE+SOMXME\nxnz62bQQGKHh/6odsiXWDrf8uRlBY0YphGmYlleMtgzWy8qm+Fh+TnwRCrxu5JcM\ntQd8ELUJDBk8FW56jP9R+2x0YZRpRD6gDnckmyyfONeB/zeqHB46daqoguWMaHIf\nHskSkpGSf8sWn9oUB8V0UwZY7pWeHeRyL47zLiQtWSYo1m7uhNCV6nRSPF18/Oc4\noDup8G6lMRetArjYS9zSvAr5E4Qr8gQU29inEn7/YqMx2FhvS5no5B2rcB3LOd3M\nCZYfagGQtmgJ7xOSBkNrQAeoBA/fczjX2kwAou/W7ZQ/axj2gJblXVzJ4GOd9Zjc\nvL++ZkPvB7kn8rYmCLE6\n=g349\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T22:29:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/commit/79969dde61ffa4a32e7074649f4f5137b3a77527","node_id":"C_kwDONqH1h9oAKDc5OTY5ZGRlNjFmZmE0YTMyZTcwNzQ2NDlmNGY1MTM3YjNhNzc1Mjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/commit/04af868fc40be836391858b546587c61646bb996","sha":"04af868fc40be836391858b546587c61646bb996","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/commits/04af868fc40be836391858b546587c61646bb996"}],"sha":"79969dde61ffa4a32e7074649f4f5137b3a77527","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/commits/79969dde61ffa4a32e7074649f4f5137b3a77527"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169448471?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mathildeshagl","id":169448471,"login":"mathildeshagl","node_id":"U_kgDOChmUFw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/commits/04af868fc40be836391858b546587c61646bb996/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T22:09:40Z","email":"mathilde.s.hagl@tum.de","name":"Mathilde Hagl"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T22:09:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Make all student details available in every participants table (#262)\n\n* Make all student details available in every participants table\n\nEvery phase''s participants table renders through CoursePhaseParticipationsTable,\nwhich only exposed first name, last name, matriculation number, login and pass\nstatus. Lecturers could therefore not see or export attributes such as email for\nthe students of a phase, unlike in the application participants table.\n\nAdd Email, Gender, Nationality, Study Degree, Study Program and Semester as\ncolumns. Email is visible by default; the rest are opt-in via the column\ndropdown so phases that already contribute extra columns stay readable. Gender,\nnationality and study degree resolve their stored codes to the displayed labels\nvia accessorFn, so sorting and search operate on the same text the lecturer\nsees.\n\nThe CSV export gains Nationality, Study Degree, Study Program and Current\nSemester; email and gender were already included.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Make the hidden participant columns reachable and align the CSV with the table\n\nThe participant columns hidden by default could not be shown: `PromptTable`\nnever rendered a column control, and `TableColumnVisibilityButton` was\nunreferenced and unexported, so neither the component nor a consumer could\nreach the hidden columns.\n\n`PromptTable` now renders that dropdown when a caller opts in via\n`enableColumnVisibilityToggle`, and the participants table opts in. Entries are\nlabelled with the column header instead of the raw id.\n\nThe CSV export also disagreed with the table: `gender`, `nationality` and\n`studyDegree` were written as stored codes (`female`, `GB`, `master`) while the\ntable rendered labels. They now go through the same label helpers, and\n`csvHeaders` is deduplicated so a phase whose data keys collide with a base\nheader (for example `studyProgram`) no longer produces two identical columns.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Maximilian Rapp <maximilian.rapp@tum.de>","tree":{"sha":"e9551c1769d020144faf959ef5d2e395ed29c6f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/git/trees/e9551c1769d020144faf959ef5d2e395ed29c6f7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-lib/git/commits/04af868fc40be836391858b546587c61646bb996","verification":{"payload":"tree e9551c1769d020144faf959ef5d2e395ed29c6f7\nparent e7db2a7aca6e18d7dd7f443cc8bc563550340ec9\nauthor Mathilde Hagl <mathilde.s.hagl@tum.de> 1788905380 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788905380 +0100\n\nMake all student details available in every participants table (#262)\n\n* Make all student details available in every participants table\n\nEvery phase''s participants table renders through CoursePhaseParticipationsTable,\nwhich only exposed first name, last name, matriculation number, login and pass\nstatus. Lecturers could therefore not see or export attributes such as email for\nthe students of a phase, unlike in the application participants table.\n\nAdd Email, Gender, Nationality, Study Degree, Study Program and Semester as\ncolumns. Email is visible by default; the rest are opt-in via the column\ndropdown so phases that already contribute extra columns stay readable. Gender,\nnationality and study degree resolve their stored codes to the displayed labels\nvia accessorFn, so sorting and search operate on the same text the lecturer\nsees.\n\nThe CSV export gains Nationality, Study Degree, Study Program and Current\nSemester; email and gender were already included.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Make the hidden participant columns reachable and align the CSV with the table\n\nThe participant columns hidden by default could not be shown: `PromptTable`\nnever rendered a column control, and `TableColumnVisibilityButton` was\nunreferenced and unexported, so neither the component nor a consumer could\nreach the hidden columns.\n\n`PromptTable` now renders that dropdown when a caller opts in via\n`enableColumnVisibilityToggle`, and the participants table opts in. Entries are\nlabelled with the column header instead of the raw id.\n\nThe CSV export also disagreed with the table: `gender`, `nationality` and\n`studyDegree` were written as stored codes (`female`, `GB`, `master`) while the\ntable rendered labels. They now go through the same label helpers, and\n`csvHeaders` is deduplicated so a phase whose data keys collide with a base\nheader (for example `studyProgram`) no longer produces two identical columns.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Maximilian Rapp <maximilian.rapp@tum.de>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoIekCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcM4QAIDaIRz+43C7KDFSjaX0wdj8\nZqygryMytUVbJ/1gUNjUq4N4+Vc3gApFzIep64PiKj1Qi19AMTsiz3EfmJlShkVB\n9YUe8OVWWsgOZRbDAPeQ5JkSgAi61E9R2VRWZ69vUMXBTTDBdeyaYLdmomE7v2Pv\npsJUOPxKVkFr+gvu57OuvE5hMybh+7GEZaal/mnEerbUEOP0YL