6c0cf9613f1538/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T09:20:04Z","email":"gu@stav.dev","name":"Gustav Hansen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T09:20:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(workbench-cli): share compatible dependencies (#1885)\n\n* fix(deps): update dependency @module-federation/vite to v1.22.0\n\n* feat(workbench-cli): share compatible dependencies\n\n* fix(workbench-cli): keep shared fallbacks deferred\n\n* perf(workbench-cli): reuse standalone builds and stop shared dependency scans early\n\n* fix(workbench-cli): reuse react across styled-components versions and isolate incompatible peers\n\n* fix(workbench-cli): isolate remote-only exposes from standalone builds\n\nLoading remote-only federation exposes during SPA discovery can emit worker bundles, so those\napps use an isolated scan while app-only builds retain reuse. Disabled sharing now reports its\nreason and uses conservative, readable checks for aliases that may rewrite shared imports.\n\n* test(workbench-cli): consolidate sharing tests in fixtures and packed-cli e2e\n\n* test(workbench-cli): separate browser dependency sharing tests\n\n* test(workbench-cli): make dependency sharing tests readable in isolation\n\nOne helper wrote every scenario''s fixture files behind five flags, so no\ntest could be read on its own. Each test now writes the files it needs and\nasserts locally, and multi-purpose tests were split by subject.\n\nThe sharing policy is a pure function, so its happy path belongs in unit\ntests instead of only being reachable through a real Vite build.","tree":{"sha":"c4838d908ddc6fb989181895cae8f1e945e092a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sanity-io/cli/git/trees/c4838d908ddc6fb989181895cae8f1e945e092a6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sanity-io/cli/git/commits/73392e660a936f126df836e7fa6c0cf9613f1538","verification":{"payload":"tree c4838d908ddc6fb989181895cae8f1e945e092a6\nparent fc1f318b2f7b4639e839a610d961fcbbdf51ac66\nauthor Gustav Hansen <gu@stav.dev> 1789982404 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789982404 +0200\n\nfeat(workbench-cli): share compatible dependencies (#1885)\n\n* fix(deps): update dependency @module-federation/vite to v1.22.0\n\n* feat(workbench-cli): share compatible dependencies\n\n* fix(workbench-cli): keep shared fallbacks deferred\n\n* perf(workbench-cli): reuse standalone builds and stop shared dependency scans early\n\n* fix(workbench-cli): reuse react across styled-components versions and isolate incompatible peers\n\n* fix(workbench-cli): isolate remote-only exposes from standalone builds\n\nLoading remote-only federation exposes during SPA discovery can emit worker bundles, so those\napps use an isolated scan while app-only builds retain reuse. Disabled sharing now reports its\nreason and uses conservative, readable checks for aliases that may rewrite shared imports.\n\n* test(workbench-cli): consolidate sharing tests in fixtures and packed-cli e2e\n\n* test(workbench-cli): separate browser dependency sharing tests\n\n* test(workbench-cli): make dependency sharing tests readable in isolation\n\nOne helper wrote every scenario''s fixture files behind five flags, so no\ntest could be read on its own. Each test now writes the files it needs and\nasserts locally, and multi-purpose tests were split by subject.\n\nThe sharing policy is a pure function, so its happy path belongs in unit\ntests instead of only being reachable through a real Vite build.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsPbECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAi2kQAIafHW+gQrqREqmhUvgatnP2\nUFzcP5UkC0mtkcpkSQSFiQEmCY6PZinlDt2Yz6L7cG/cFNJRoYHDObQTeR7LLBoO\n8N45voj4IH8bM7G4Wm2GPKAxIQCcMxLWc1VmwtMKsC7USeHdmBZwd9WAQDvgdhzp\nfsQsG/IRVrLRO0YUxSt6KoPNUkAAX0nk+d2SUzo77MOr3eR+TkrdB33QMbdeChAT\nat7Y+SnwgtX31d2Xd9wJxtPEz1z++lUgDTYK2MeLtZ/YBcqBKqdYYXpQCRdLToTr\nKCr0xhK4TggZsfg7QTkmDYQ1eqgnPZeJNl55llh5vhD6SiqI4V0F6dnvicY/jZQ8\n/7s9VFpdTib0M+rA1lfryTS2z2bbvlEA/2HUS7n8