url":"https://api.github.com/users/tbeseda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tbeseda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tbeseda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tbeseda","id":15697,"login":"tbeseda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1Njk3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tbeseda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tbeseda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tbeseda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tbeseda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tbeseda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tbeseda","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sanity-io/cli/commits/26b1282c819920fa842a09c65a7a93d044838f7c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T14:08:20Z","email":"tbeseda@gmail.com","name":"Taylor Beseda"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T14:08:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(e2e): disable npm audit and fund lookups in e2e installs (#1849)\n\nEvery `sanity init` under test runs a real `npm install`, and the audit\nadvisory lookup plus the funding notice each add a registry round trip\nthat the tests do not exercise. When the registry is slow those trips\npush the install past the 120s test timeout.\n\nSet `npm_config_audit` and `npm_config_fund` to `false` in two places:\nthe e2e `runCli` harness, so local runs get it too, and the workflow job\nenv, so the packed-CLI install in the global setup gets it as well.","tree":{"sha":"cb711c25a1eef6d37c4406574e301295c6baa4e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sanity-io/cli/git/trees/cb711c25a1eef6d37c4406574e301295c6baa4e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sanity-io/cli/git/commits/26b1282c819920fa842a09c65a7a93d044838f7c","verification":{"payload":"tree cb711c25a1eef6d37c4406574e301295c6baa4e0\nparent 48fa623dd56cf82bdb4bb3d5c76161face016715\nauthor Taylor Beseda <tbeseda@gmail.com> 1788530900 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788530900 -0600\n\nchore(e2e): disable npm audit and fund lookups in e2e installs (#1849)\n\nEvery `sanity init` under test runs a real `npm install`, and the audit\nadvisory lookup plus the funding notice each add a registry round trip\nthat the tests do not exercise. When the registry is slow those trips\npush the install past the 120s test timeout.\n\nSet `npm_config_audit` and `npm_config_fund` to `false` in two places:\nthe e2e `runCli` harness, so local runs get it too, and the workflow job\nenv, so the packed-CLI install in the global setup gets it as well.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmtDUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAInwQAHZL5q2AwCmjbi7wvpCJRn5O\nxYh9EojKMO6fAdQp0D+p1kIzZsL/4d4rfeyhuOHWtIhNJKozuX3S36P43DL1gDtk\n6lAt9fSCGE3FG1ZiA6qQ1hIfJXkwB58uqUDkphYMX47ItJRh8V1xbsmRZMew8/hP\nOvTTirgROaql9S1xAlxx46R4HHBmUeHLbYYQjnf/G9ZEN1Ol/VoROLSBXHlobgSq\ncQOUdqtf3vBQOsimWMkzyR7LIzNEpkD72ONoE1CxXwgBOn75g0zg9ZqosKNB7nA9\nYm5ogQuU93DqrKBLzt2Ror4oiP1lr/4i4w6e8McWCQa9CZgMmqIavRalMaKLycDs\ny92kZ0YXayfNaNdaTgdi1Zq+NOmmVGtuAbppOZo/cMqBZEXXisRtxFtQZynQdX/m\nE6vJdejjFMjnBbSC/RGK9WeLT1jC8vagZyme0rEuEl7BGSheBFjI9WsZvKVf/x9z\nEVz2dm92vDRzmtekYymS0j6axXYhQ81gnROdU0yZRGYjWeUvBVuwpd0PH/P+9F7T\npbdgafLPgS2OzXypkgyi87gSlm4R6HQRid0gFwJfyFfsMmEmU4R+i3m0x5xGIbZU\niN7TGQW0NMPxocUO3LAoc2aKb1Fnd1rzFyO+9bEgAsmtNaJL2g2Zj3INgY3kcxVc\neU3OSBelS7FhwkN7uNxZ\n=Uvh3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-04T14:08:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sanity-io/cli/commit/26b1282c819920fa842a09c65a7a93d044838f7c","node_id":"C_kwDONqSnoNoAKDI2YjEyODJjODE5OTIwZmE4NDJhMDljNjVhN2E5M2QwNDQ4MzhmN2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sanity-io/cli/commit/48fa623dd56cf82bdb4bb3d5c76161face016715","sha":"48fa623dd56cf82bdb4bb3d5c76161face016715","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sanity-io/cli/commits/48fa623dd56cf82bdb4bb3d5c76161face016715"}],"sha":"26b1282c819920fa842a09c65a7a93d044838f7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sanity-io/cli/commits/26b1282c819920fa842a09c65a7a93d044838f7c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15697?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tbeseda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tbeseda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tbeseda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tbeseda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tbeseda","id":15697,"login":"tbeseda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1Njk3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tbeseda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tbeseda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tbeseda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tbeseda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tbeseda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tbeseda","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sanity-io/cli/commits/48fa623dd56cf82bdb4bb3d5c76161face016715/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T14:08:05Z","email":"tbeseda@gmail.com","name":"Taylor Beseda"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T14:08:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(cli-core): accept numbers and Dates in formatDateTime, add formattElapsed (#1848)\n\n* feat(cli-core): accept numbers and Dates in formatDateTime, add formatElapsed\n\n`formatDateTime` now takes `Date | number | string`, so callers that hold epoch\nmilliseconds or a `Date` no longer round-trip through `toISOString()`, which\nthrows on an invalid value. An unparseable string is still returned as-is; an\ninvalid `Date` or non-finite number formats as an empty string.\n\n`formatElapsed` is a precise companion to the approximate `formatDuration`,\nfor output such as how long an operation took: `450ms`, `12s`, `1m 30s`,\n`2h 5m`, `3d 7h`.\n\n* fix(cli-core): round elapsed milliseconds before choosing a unit\n\n`formatElapsed` compared the raw value against one second and rounded\nafterwards, so 999.6ms rendered as `1000ms`. Round to whole milliseconds\nfirst so the unit boundary holds for fractional input such as\n`performance.now()` timings.","tree":{"sha":"3d87311f3f99eecd1a6cd79730d7d0c26a9525a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sanity-io/cli/git/trees/3d87311f3f99eecd1a6cd79730d7d0c26a9525a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sanity-io/cli/git/commits/48fa623dd56cf82bdb4bb3d5c76161face016715","verification":{"payload":"tree 3d87311f3f99eecd1a6cd79730d7d0c26a9525a7\nparent 67f31e3227c5cb118ccc452986d3950254b7b754\nauthor Taylor Beseda <tbeseda@gmail.com> 1788530885 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788530885 -0600\n\nfeat(cli-core): accept numbers and Dates in formatDateTime, add formattElapsed (#1848)\n\n* feat(cli-core): accept numbers and Dates in formatDateTime, add formatElapsed\n\n`formatDateTime` now takes `Date | number | string`, so callers that hold epoch\nmilliseconds or a `Date` no longer round-trip through `toISOString()`, which\nthrows on an invalid value. An unparseable string is still returned as-is; an\ninvalid `Date` or non-finite number formats as an empty string.\n\n`formatElapsed` is a precise companion to the approximate `formatDuration`,\nfor output such as how long an operation took: `450ms`, `12s`, `1m 30s`,\n`2h 5m`, `3d 7h`.\n\n* fix(cli-core): round elapsed milliseconds before choosing a unit\n\n`formatElapsed` compared the raw value against one second and rounded\nafterwards, so 999.6ms rendered as `1000ms`. Round to whole milliseconds\nfirst so the unit boundary holds for fractional input such as\n`performance.now()` timings.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmtDFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACdQQAEQ1ARwvAWUsuHxLvVg6i7Kc\nY+Y6cIEiUsJwQQDrg8iPm51lxnGtOaXzROxLlYDmT0QXGiCKmZxqVMrNAt8mVDsQ\n+/eoi3hZNd/wRIaibtRZ8fsqdKvqlu8No2xIa2viPGXXJdy39KoXuknPPvvIeofP\n8JvGNOtoYNYB93WQJu2nHLfJ/gO8xc2TnxwyMG2om3YMGGoiHFup3SVJ8Lqbduqf\nNMbOowP3mqXB1zn0BpwUmzuJN2ba9Q2ApfPxmaEg1fk/ReZg3X4quZsuf7HST1w2\n2+/x6WrX6sH149Y1HBvgLmBsaeDk3PNcWCqTb+8vdOomg+llZC1HlsFxT+WDCBtE\niNLFlL8KPUhI1rThsbFKDx9M4zan0Q4sW6XbC3ytq89ZAb/blM/VQMXC67ajC2uO\n9CXxieerraeAyijV8dKsnU0JvmAD0bchQthxZIwSSKkb+H9lGI8FWPYN0q2CTAUM\nLuvExZ5MA/6udJjU9bb0npKf3frj7aB9ppzCtm84EtuVWsWpelMaO8x5vOzjD5+U\nvoOqRlqw3RnqqOB9/lKcw1GNGdYCGFlS8qGpuRfeUr5W4r6t/rZwiwFWGgA1St4M\nhYcOxzSZO2cDbnylIALyorGmpDThfPLrcKZufz5qd8J7/9JEiRpUTnIDSj9OW15H\nxBWC7IqJ79FzOn1xRwj1\n=IzAJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-04T14:08:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-fl