riptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redhat-developer/rhdh-plugin-export-overlays/commit/a3543699f3a6d4c04903fef5bf8ba1f3ca38859c","node_id":"C_kwDONrRnPNoAKGEzNTQzNjk5ZjNhNmQ0YzA0OTAzZmVmNWJmOGJhMWYzY2EzODg1OWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redhat-developer/rhdh-plugin-export-overlays/commit/bab8a8f6e8138ff7bcf154cad12a91e2e41bf8fc","sha":"bab8a8f6e8138ff7bcf154cad12a91e2e41bf8fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-plugin-export-overlays/commits/bab8a8f6e8138ff7bcf154cad12a91e2e41bf8fc"}],"sha":"a3543699f3a6d4c04903fef5bf8ba1f3ca38859c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-plugin-export-overlays/commits/a3543699f3a6d4c04903fef5bf8ba1f3ca38859c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/139310?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christoph-jerolimov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christoph-jerolimov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christoph-jerolimov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christoph-jerolimov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/christoph-jerolimov","id":139310,"login":"christoph-jerolimov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTMxMA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christoph-jerolimov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christoph-jerolimov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christoph-jerolimov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christoph-jerolimov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christoph-jerolimov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/christoph-jerolimov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-plugin-export-overlays/commits/bab8a8f6e8138ff7bcf154cad12a91e2e41bf8fc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T12:53:20Z","email":"jerolimov+git@redhat.com","name":"Christoph Jerolimov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T12:53:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(orchestrator): replace MinIO with RustFS for the Loki e2e object storage (#4119)\n\n* test(orchestrator): replace MinIO with RustFS for the Loki e2e object storage\n\nThe orchestrator Loki install script deployed MinIO as the S3 backend for\nLokiStack and bootstrapped the bucket with a separate `mc` Job. Switch the\nbackend to RustFS (quay.io/rustfs/rustfs:1.0.1), an S3-compatible store with\nno console or client image requirement.\n\n- Rename every LOKI_MINIO_* variable, MINIO_* shell variable and function to\n  their RUSTFS counterparts; MinIO is no longer referenced anywhere.\n- Configure RustFS through RUSTFS_ACCESS_KEY / RUSTFS_SECRET_KEY from the\n  credentials Secret, bind only the S3 API port, disable the console and log\n  to stdout (the image''s /logs is not writable under an arbitrary OpenShift\n  uid). Readiness uses the /health endpoint.\n- Drop the create-bucket Job. RustFS has no startup bucket option, but its\n  image ships curl and PUT Bucket is idempotent, so ensure_rustfs_bucket now\n  creates the bucket over the S3 API from inside the RustFS pod via oc exec,\n  with credentials taken from the pod environment.\n\nVerified locally against the real image running as a non-root uid: /health\nand /health/ready return 200, PUT Bucket returns 200 for new and existing\nbuckets, wrong credentials return 403. The rendered Secret, Service and\nDeployment manifests parse as valid YAML; shellcheck is clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Christoph Jerolimov <jerolimov+git@redhat.com>\n\n* fix(orchestrator): align metadata OCI tags with Backstage 1.54.9\n\nThe orchestrator Package metadata still referenced bs_1.54.6 artifact tags\nwhile the repo tracks Backstage 1.54.9, so the e2e deploy would pull images\nfor the wrong Backstage version. Update all five dynamicArtifact tags.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Christoph Jerolimov <jerolimov+git@redhat.com>\n\n* fix(orchestrator): harden Loki helper error message extraction\n\nAvoid empty Error.message falling through when formatting Loki probe failures.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nSigned-off-by: Christoph Jerolimov <jerolimov+git@redhat.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Christoph Jerolimov <jerolimov+git@redhat.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"3f2aff830001ba4330d72f16b8215c6f29df81a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-plugin-export-overlays/git/trees/3f2aff830001ba4330d72f16b8215c6f29df81a6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-plugin-export-overlays/git/commits/bab8a8f6e8138ff7bcf154cad12a91e2e41bf8fc","verification":{"payload":"tree 3f2aff830001ba4330d72f16b8215c6f29df81a6\nparent db830617817e527eb407c42fb90c881652e55cca\nauthor Christoph Jerolimov <jerolimov+git@redhat.com> 1791464000 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791464000 +0200\n\ntest(orchestrator): replace MinIO with RustFS for the Loki e2e object storage (#4119)\n\n* test(orchestrator): replace MinIO with RustFS for the Loki e2e object storage\n\nThe orchestrator Loki install script deployed MinIO as the S3 backend for\nLokiStack and bootstrapped the bucket with a separate `mc` Job. Switch the\nbackend to RustFS (quay.io/rustfs/rustfs:1.0.1), an S3-compatible store with\nno console or client image requirement.\n\n- Rename every LOKI_MINIO_* variable, MINIO_* shell variable and function to\n  their RUSTFS counterparts; MinIO is no longer referenced anywhere.\n- Configure RustFS through RUSTFS_ACCESS_KEY / RUSTFS_SECRET_KEY from the\n  credentials Secret, bind only the S3 API port, disable the console and log\n  to stdout (the image''s /logs is not writable under an arbitrary OpenShift\n  uid). Readiness uses the /health endpoint.\n- Drop the create-bucket Job. RustFS has no startup bucket option, but its\n  image ships curl and PUT Bucket is idempotent, so ensure_rustfs_bucket now\n  creates the bucket over the S3 API from inside the RustFS pod via oc exec,\n  with credentials taken from the pod environment.\n\nVerified locally against the real image running as a non-root uid: /health\nand /health/ready return 200, PUT Bucket returns 200 for new and existing\nbuckets, wrong credentials return 403. The rendered Secret, Service and\nDeployment manifests parse as valid YAML; shellcheck is clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Christoph Jerolimov <jerolimov+git@redhat.com>\n\n* fix(orchestrator): align metadata OCI tags with Backstage 1.54.9\n\nThe orchestrator Package metadata still referenced bs_1.54.6 artifact tags\nwhile the repo tracks Backstage 1.54.9, so the e2e deploy would pull images\nfor the wrong Backstage version. Update all five dynamicArtifact tags.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Christoph Jerolimov <jerolimov+git@redhat.com>\n\n* fix(orchestrator): harden Loki helper error message extraction\n\nAvoid empty Error.message falling through when formatting Loki probe failures.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nSigned-off-by: Christoph Jerolimov <jerolimov+git@redhat.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Christoph Jerolimov <jerolimov+git@redhat.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx5JACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0sgQAEhVc+bqrKbj9EU0k46/1khE\nkEiatyrcmxOFi5sCW5nphnBIxSyNCx/hzwmOTxkjYTqLe4VNj9peL/PTQQRclr97\nJy9Hrtegp7TTqbCuh/3vVgB05R+7z8zbQOhS4NPv