db66302e7fb4b1c21d38e9a703660","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-plugin-export-overlays/commits/a4101f07978db66302e7fb4b1c21d38e9a703660"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-plugin-export-overlays/commits/b237f68f6803b97ca5a251d9d5c992d2080c320d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T16:32:55Z","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T16:32:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Update `app-defaults` workspace to commit `bd06342` for backstage `1.54.6` on branch `main` (#3877)\n\n* Update `app-defaults` workspace to commit `06e72b2` for backstage `1.54.6` on branch `main`\n\n* fix(e2e): allow Red Hat PostgreSQL image for Helm deploy\n\nBitnami subchart in RHDH chart 2.0-90-CI rejects registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-15 unless global.security.allowInsecureImages is true.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): disable intelligentAssistant sidecar\n\nChart 2.0-90-CI defaults intelligentAssistant.enabled=true and starts lightspeed-core with --synthesized-config-output (CrashLoop). global.lightspeed.enabled is ignored.\n\n* Update `app-defaults` workspace to commit `bdadab2` for backstage `1.54.6` on branch `main`\n\n* Update `app-defaults` workspace to commit `bd06342` for backstage `1.54.6` on branch `main`\n\n* fix(e2e): remove obsolete allowInsecureImages config\n\nRemove global.security.allowInsecureImages as the midstream commit\ncausing the PostgreSQL image verification issue has been reverted.\n\nSuggested-by: rm3l <rm3l@users.noreply.github.com>\nAssisted-By: opencode\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* fix(e2e): disable built-in nav-content:app extension\n\nDisable the built-in nav-content:app extension in app-config-rhdh.yaml\nto resolve the EXTENSION_ATTACHMENT_CONFLICT with app-defaults''s\nnav-content:app/sidebar extension when running against images that\nstill include midstream navModule (prior to rhdh#5533).\n\nAssisted-By: opencode\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* fix(e2e): align dynamic-plugins tags with backstage 1.54.6\n\nUpdate app-defaults and github-provider package tags to bs_1.54.6\nto align with the workspace Backstage version.\n\nAssisted-By: opencode\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Christoph Jerolimov <jerolimov+git@redhat.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"f9b689f9789d0476f08c8dee819b97554b37a891","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-plugin-export-overlays/git/trees/f9b689f9789d0476f08c8dee819b97554b37a891"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-plugin-export-overlays/git/commits/b237f68f6803b97ca5a251d9d5c992d2080c320d","verification":{"payload":"tree f9b689f9789d0476f08c8dee819b97554b37a891\nparent bae3d55ceebef157c3ddadd6f3dfa3aa55c6c9d3\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1790785975 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790785975 +0530\n\nUpdate `app-defaults` workspace to commit `bd06342` for backstage `1.54.6` on branch `main` (#3877)\n\n* Update `app-defaults` workspace to commit `06e72b2` for backstage `1.54.6` on branch `main`\n\n* fix(e2e): allow Red Hat PostgreSQL image for Helm deploy\n\nBitnami subchart in RHDH chart 2.0-90-CI rejects registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-15 unless global.security.allowInsecureImages is true.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): disable intelligentAssistant sidecar\n\nChart 2.0-90-CI defaults intelligentAssistant.enabled=true and starts lightspeed-core with --synthesized-config-output (CrashLoop). global.lightspeed.enabled is ignored.\n\n* Update `app-defaults` workspace to commit `bdadab2` for backstage `1.54.6` on branch `main`\n\n* Update `app-defaults` workspace to commit `bd06342` for backstage `1.54.6` on branch `main`\n\n* fix(e2e): remove obsolete allowInsecureImages config\n\nRemove global.security.allowInsecureImages as the midstream commit\ncausing the PostgreSQL image verification issue has been reverted.\n\nSuggested-by: rm3l <rm3l@users.noreply.github.com>\nAssisted-By: opencode\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* fix(e2e): disable built-in nav-content:app extension\n\nDisable the built-in nav-content:app extension in app-config-rhdh.yaml\nto resolve the EXTENSION_ATTACHMENT_CONFLICT with app-defaults''s\nnav-content:app/sidebar extension when running against images that\nstill include midstream navModule (prior to rhdh#5533).\n\nAssisted-By: opencode\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* fix(e2e): align dynamic-plugins tags with backstage 1.54.6\n\nUpdate app-defaults and github-provider package tags to bs_1.54.6\nto align with the workspace Backstage version.\n\nAssisted-By: opencode\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Christoph Jerolimov <jerolimov+git@redhat.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvTm3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWLMQAGMkOD1SAkFMLjQPFBBIBD5N\nXHAULYkqu2zQzz0TtzALv1e9zqzuGYrtlsIwuRejgUoWbFo0aYyP6mEOeF/1Wagh\nfBsEkyRLoRltax3goayN8qMLuXrqtN4fme46SUqcrqADipMz0zHBIU1yqFCQ+9cR\nfGYwy0OyrN3LN0VrbIllp6xrRjGKhee7dleRQdfIndBRaSePSi9reAV+1rFaz1h2\nc+85SzsWQboWTrtSf0noaEj5KdtSGs/b4wNXfXa6cxSqpdbLzDnn/CjRxh5H3lDB\n2c1CFzBjfP8CRle6RMcYa0L+j4VulleBkHuLTSv4NLWbHuG6uEnQhF3qlpZhl4z1\njaTZfWMckRDJoQXTwCh0qd3rVlVfcT6tp2ZfSpPYgaen67wIkcrO7OXjqkuBupfF\n2OSIKL0tvCCrBQIsxeq16FsxSE/FvhNoyAjO8wT4iE2URmd2XXG7wT2fms3vdnZY\n+LYuG6Wei5C9Mu3/A/rnuSKVn5TsUf7nohr7tA5YV6TdGtQozru6oMph1CU8wcPk\nxyoNFEdYXRbTcuif/w5+H0qDcgrjx8+WfLEcOXTNyjxmlQO6Bs9i8+kioyovFFnv\n6sHxreotycZrKVJxnEeATeL9bd6OZ+HOCATeNpMxg4ue/F+naGFDGx/XatlPpurQ\n9wA1OQUxEz0fhXXq/1kL\n=cKyZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T16:32:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redhat-developer/rhdh-plugin-export-overlays/commit/b237f68f6803b97ca5a251d9d5c992d2080c320d","node_id":"C_kwDONrRnPNoAKGIyMzdmNjhmNjgwM2I5N2NhNWEyNTFkOWQ1Yzk5MmQyMDgwYzMyMGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redhat-developer/rhdh-plugin-export-overlays/commit/bae3d55ceebef157c3ddadd6f3dfa3aa55c6c9d3","sha":"bae3d55ceebef157c3ddadd6f3dfa3aa55c6c9d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-plugin-export-overlays/commits/bae3d55ceebef157c3ddadd6f3dfa3aa55c6c9d3"}],"sha":"b237f68f6803b97ca5a251d9d5c992d2080c320d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-plugin-export-overlays/commits/b237f68f6803b97ca5a251d9d5c992d2080c320d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1463004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gustavolira","id":1463004,"login":"gustavolira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NjMwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-plugin-export-overlays/commits/bae3d55ceebef157c3ddadd6f3dfa3aa55c6c9d3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T15:28:45Z","email":"guga.java@gmail.com","name":"Gustavo Lira e Silva"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T15:28:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(app-defaults): restore 2 of 3 nightly tests, install the GitHub auth provider (#3419)\n\n* test(app-defaults): drop the nightly skip whose reason no longer holds\n\nThe whole suite — all three tests — has been skipped in nightly since\nRHIDP-15482, on the grounds that DPDY `{{inherit}}` had nothing to resolve\nagainst because app-auth and app-integrations were not in the RHDH image. That\nticket is Closed and the premise is now false at both ends.\n\nChecked the published index rather than inferring it from the ticket. Pulled\nquay.io/rhdh/plugin-catalog-index:next (--override-arch amd64, no arm64 variant\nexists) and its dynamic-plugins.default.yaml carries all three, enabled and\ndigest-pinned, built 2026-08-19:\n\n  red-hat-developer-hub-backstage-plugin-app-auth          enabled: true\n  red-hat-developer-hub-backstage-plugin-app-defaults      enabled: true\n  red-hat-developer-hub-backstage-plugin-app-integrations  enabled: true\n\nAnd the other end matches: in nightly mode e2e-test-utils emits\n`oci://${registry}/${displayName}:{{inherit}}`, where the default registry is\nquay.io/rhdh and toDisplayName(''@red-hat-developer-hub/backstage-plugin-app-auth'')\ngives exactly the name above. Registry, name and enabled state all line up, so\nthere is something for `{{inherit}}` to resolve to.\n\nWhat I cannot do is run the nightly — that needs a cluster. So this restores the\nlane and lets the nightly answer. If it comes back red the skip returns with an\naccurate reason, which is already better than the stale one it carries now:\napp-defaults'' only project is app-defaults-app-next, so today the skip leaves\nthat workspace with no nightly coverage at all.\n\nVerified: tsc, eslint and prettier clean in workspaces/app-defaults/e2e-tests.\n\n* fix(app-defaults): install the GitHub auth provider the e2e suite signs in with\n\nThe third spec drives the session-auth API for `github`, but the backend never\nhad that provider. `/api/auth/github/start` answers 404 with\n`{\"error\":{\"name\":\"NotFoundError\",\"message\":\"Unknown auth provider ''github''\"}}`\n— which is what the popup contains when the test times out waiting for it to\nreach github.com — and the backend log confirms it, registering only\n`Configuring auth provider: oidc` and `guest`.\n\n`auth.providers.github` in app-config-rhdh.yaml only CONFIGURES a provider. The\nbackend module has to be installed as a dynamic plugin, and RHDH''s default list\ndoes not carry it: the install log shows the auth modules present are keycloak,\nguest and oidc, with no github one even in the disabled set. Per rhdh:docs/auth.md\nthe provider comes from an overlay package this repo publishes, which is what is\nadded here. It was never installed — the test and its app-config landed together\nin aaa32ef6 and the workspace has never had a dynamic-plugins.yaml — so the test\nhas been asserting a provider that was not there since it was written.\n\nThe e2e-test-utils `auth: \"github\"` preset installs the same package, but it also\nsets `signInPage: github`, which would replace the OIDC/Keycloak sign-in this\nsuite logs in with. So the module is added directly rather than by switching the\npreset.\n\nWhy the workspace''s own three packages are re-listed here: adding this file\nSUPPRESSES the auto-generation from metadata/. `_buildDynamicPluginsConfig` in\ne2e-test-utils takes the user config INSTEAD of the metadata-derived one, and\n`injectMetadataConfig` only maps over entries already present, so it never adds\nthem back. Verified against 2.1.11 rather than assumed: a file listing only the\nprovider resolves to a single-plugin deployment with all three app-defaults\npackages gone. Re-listing them is also what every other workspace carrying this\nfile already does — acr, topology, tekton, scorecard and eleven more.\n\nVerified the resulting plugin list through the package''s own\nprocessPluginsForDeployment: the three app-defaults entries come out identical to\ntoday''s auto-generated output, pluginConfig included, plus the provider with its\ncredentials intact.\n\nThis fixes one of the two failures on this PR. The other — the Catalog sidebar\nlink being unclickable because the sticky global-header covers it — is a\nseparate, layout-level problem and is not addressed here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(app-defaults): mark the Catalog click expected-to-fail on RHDHBUGS-3627\n\nThe suite''s remaining failure is not a test problem. The global header is a\nsticky MuiAppBar with z-index 1100 and the sidebar list starts at the top of the\nviewport, so its first item — Catalog — renders underneath it. Playwright\nretried the click for 10 seconds, 21 attempts, each reporting the element\nvisible, enabled, stable and scrolled into view, then blocked by\n`<nav id=\"global-header\">`. The screenshot confirms it: the first visible\nsidebar entry is Create, and Catalog is nowhere on screen while the\naccessibility tree has it as the first sidebar child. A user with a mouse cannot\nopen Catalog either.\n\nThat is RHDHBUGS-3627, which absorbed RHDHBUGS-3573 (\"Global header overlaps top\ncontent of sidebar navigation\") — the exact symptom here. The video, screenshots\nand an offline reproduction recipe are attached to that ticket. Its fix,\nredhat-developer/rhdh-plugins#4405, is still open, so no image the e2e lanes\npull carries it yet.\n\n`test.fail`, not `test.skip`, and that is the point of this commit rather than\nan implementation detail. This PR exists because a skip went stale: it cited\nRHIDP-15482, the ticket closed, nobody re-read the test, and the workspace sat\nwith no nightly coverage for months. Replacing one skip with another would\nrebuild the same debt against a different ticket.\n\n`fail` does not have that failure mode. Verified against the runner this repo\npins (@playwright/test 1.59.1) rather than assumed:\n\n  - while the bug exists: the test reports ✘ but the run is green, and the\n    other two tests keep running — so nightly coverage is restored for them.\n  - once the bug is fixed: \"Expected to fail, but passed.\" → the run goes red\n    until someone deletes the marker.\n\nCI becomes the reminder instead of a person. Applied unconditionally rather than\ngated on E2E_NIGHTLY_MODE, because the overlap breaks the PR check too.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(app-defaults): record why the expected-failure is not a flake\n\nReview feedback on #3419: the unconditional test.fail could report \"Expected to\nfail, but passed\" if the overlap turned out to depend on runner viewport or\ntiming, which would read as brittleness rather than as the reminder firing.\n\nIt does not. From the failing run''s artifacts: 23 click attempts over 10s, every\none blocked by `<nav id=\"global-header\">`, none succeeding — and reproduced at\nboth 1920x1080 (screenshot) and 1280x720 (video). The overlap is geometric.\n\nNoting it in the comment so whoever hits the red knows to look for the fix\nhaving landed rather than for a flake.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(app-defaults): use `enabled: true`, the field the install CLI asks for\n\nReview feedback on #3419. The repo is mixed — 10 of the 15 workspaces carrying a\ndynamic-plugins.yaml use `enabled`, 5 use `disabled` — but the tie-breaker is\nnot the count. `isPluginDisabled` in the install CLI treats them as equivalent\nand then says which it wants:\n\n    if (hasEnabled && hasDisabled) {\n      warn(`... specifies both ''enabled'' and ''disabled''. The ''enabled'' field\n            takes precedence; please use only ''enabled''.`);\n\nSo `enabled: true` is what the tool asks for, and following the majority happens\nto agree with it rather than the other way round.\n\nRe-ran the plugin resolution after the change: same four packages, the three\napp-defaults ones still identical to the metadata-generated output, and the\nprovider''s credentials intact.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(app-defaults): use test.skip, matching the documented convention\n\nReview feedback on #3419: `test.fail` had no prior use anywhere in the repo, and\nAGENTS.md prescribes `test.skip` for a known product bug. Switching to `skip`\nrather than introducing a second pattern by side-effect — a repo-wide convention\nis a decision for the team to take deliberately, not one a PR about an\napp-defaults skip should make on its way past.\n\nThis gives up the property `fail` had: it turned the run red with \"Expected to\nfail, but passed\" the day the bug was fixed, so CI was the reminder. A skip\ncannot do that — verified rather than assumed, the run is byte-identical whether\nthe bug is present or not.\n\nSince nothing in this repo will notice the fix landing, the reminder is split\nacross both ends and the comment says so plainly:\n\n  - here, a REMOVE THIS note naming RHDHBUGS-3627 and rhdh-plugins#4405, and\n    stating outright that no signal will arrive;\n  - on RHDHBUGS-3627, a comment pointing back at this file, so whoever closes\n    the ticket is told there is a test to unskip.\n\nThat pair is weaker than a red build and the comment does not pretend otherwise.\nIt is, at least, aimed at an OPEN ticket with a linked upstream fix, which is\nthe part the RHIDP-15482 skip got wrong: it cited a ticket that closed, and the\nstaleness went unnoticed for months.\n\nKept unconditional rather than gated on E2E_NIGHTLY_MODE, because the overlap\nbreaks the PR check too.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(app-defaults): give the skip a root-cause summary, not a bare ticket id\n\nReview feedback on #3419. AGENTS.md prescribes `test.skip(condition, \"<root\ncause summary>\")`, and the repo''s other conditional skips follow it — homepage\nwrites \"homepage-backend defaultWidgets are not supported on NFS yet\". A bare\n\"RHDHBUGS-3627\" was the only one that made a reader open Jira to learn what is\nbroken.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(app-defaults): stop duplicating the plugins the app-next layer already ships\n\nThe e2e run on 5477fc66 never reached a test. The install init container aborted\nand the pod came up Init:Error, so RHDH never started:\n\n    InstallException: Duplicate OCI plugin configuration for\n    oci://…/red-hat-developer-hub-backstage-plugin-app-auth!…\n    found at the same level in dynamic-plugins.yaml:\n    oci://…/app-auth:pr_3419__0.1.1__coverage!…\n\nMy doing. The file listed all three of the workspace''s packages on the reasoning\nthat a user config suppresses the metadata auto-generation — true — but two of\nthem were already coming from somewhere else. The new-frontend-system layer\nships app-auth and app-integrations, and it is merged in automatically because\nthis project''s namespace ends in `-app-next`.\n\nThey did not collapse into one entry because the two merge paths do not dedupe\nalike. `_mergeGeneratedWithBase` passes `normalizeKey:\ngetNormalizedPluginMergeKey`, which collapses the same plugin across differing\ntags; `_mergeBaseConfigs`, which is the path a user config takes, keys on the raw\n`package` string alone. So `app-auth:bs_1.49.4__0.0.1` from that layer and\n`app-auth:bs_1.52.0__0.1.1` from this file survived as two entries, then\n`resolvePluginPackages` rewrote both to the same pr_ ref — and the installer\nrejects that.\n\nOnly `app-defaults` and the provider are listed now. Both omissions are load\nbearing, so the file says why rather than leaving the next person to rediscover\nit by breaking the deployment again.\n\nThe earlier verification missed this because it simulated\n`processPluginsForDeployment` on the file alone — the step where the layers are\nmerged was never exercised. Redone over the full path this time, replaying\n`_mergeBaseConfigs` with the same three base layers and merge options the\ndeployment uses:\n\n  - before: 10 plugins, app-auth and app-integrations duplicated\n  - after: 8 plugins, no duplicates\n  - against main''s current behaviour: an identical 7-plugin set plus the\n    provider, which is the whole intended delta\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(app-defaults): override backstage compatibility to 1.54.4\n\n* test(app-defaults): trim the comments, drop the stale backstage pin\n\nReview findings on this branch:\n\n- The comments were 27 of 44 lines in `dynamic-plugins.yaml` — the highest\n  ratio of any e2e config in the repo — and near-verbatim copies of the\n  commit messages they came from. The rationale belongs in the commit and\n  the PR body; the file keeps the two facts a reader needs at that line.\n\n- `backstage.json` pinned 1.54.4 while `source.json` says 1.52.1 and the\n  metadata says `bs_1.52.0__`. It came from an `/override-backstage` run\n  whose metadata refresh failed, so the pin landed and nothing else did,\n  making this the only workspace whose pin is a minor off its own metadata.\n  It is not inert: `bootstrapPluginBuilds.py` only uses a workspace''s own\n  version when the workspace is flagged outdated, and that check is\n  minor-only — the pin clears the flag, so the next bootstrap would emit\n  `bs_1.54.6__` tags against e2e entries hardcoded at `bs_1.52.0__`.\n  Removing it leaves `source.json` to keep the workspace correctly flagged.\n\n- `signIn.resolvers: usernameMatchingUserEntityName` contradicted the doc\n  the comment cites: GitHub is here for the session-auth API only, Keycloak\n  owns sign-in, and the spec closes the popup at github.com without ever\n  completing the handshake. Removed, so GitHub cannot issue an identity.\n\n- `clientId`/`clientSecret` were declared in both `app-config-rhdh.yaml` and\n  the plugin''s `pluginConfig`. The provider block now lives in one file,\n  with `callbackUrl` alongside the credentials it belongs to.\n\nAlso merged main: the branch was 49 commits behind and its last green e2e\npredates two of its own commits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"be9b2e87735a250c382f4320cdf30bd20ed00434","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-plugin-export-overlays/git/trees/be9b2e87735a250c382f4320cdf30bd20ed00434"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-plugin-export-overlays/git/commits/bae3d55ceebef157c3ddadd6f3dfa3aa55c6c9d3","verification":{"payload":"tree be9b2e87735a250c382f4320cdf30bd20ed00434\nparent 646d983f0a6b3ae10061046e540ecf058d23de3c\nauthor Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com> 1790782125 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790782125 -0400\n\ntest(app-defaults): restore 2 of 3 nightly tests, install the GitHub auth provider (#3419)\n\n* test(app-defaults): drop the nightly skip whose reason no longer holds\n\nThe whole suite — all three tests — has been skipped in nightly since\nRHIDP-15482, on the grounds that DPDY `{{inherit}}` had nothing to resolve\nagainst because app-auth and app-integrations were not in the RHDH image. That\nticket is Closed and the premise is now false at both ends.\n\nChecked the published index rather than inferring it from the ticket. Pulled\nquay.io/rhdh/plugin-catalog-index:next (--override-arch amd64, no arm64 variant\nexists) and its dynamic-plugins.default.yaml carries all three, enabled and\ndigest-pinned, built 2026-08-19:\n\n  red-hat-developer-hub-backstage-plugin-app-auth          enabled: true\n  red-hat-developer-hub-backstage-plugin-app-defaults      enabled: true\n  red-hat-developer-hub-backstage-plugin-app-integrations  enabled: true\n\nAnd the other end matches: in nightly mode e2e-test-utils emits\n`oci://${registry}/${displayName}:{{inherit}}`, where the default registry is\nquay.io/rhdh and toDisplayName(''@red-hat-developer-hub/backstage-plugin-app-auth'')\ngives exactly the name above. Registry, name and enabled state all line up, so\nthere is something for `{{inherit}}` to resolve to.\n\nWhat I cannot do is run the nightly — that needs a cluster. So this restores the\nlane and lets the nightly answer. If it comes back red the skip returns with an\naccurate reason, which is already better than the stale one it carries now:\napp-defaults'' only project is app-defaults-app-next, so today the skip leaves\nthat workspace with no nightly coverage at all.\n\nVerified: tsc, eslint and prettier clean in workspaces/app-defaults/e2e-tests.\n\n* fix(app-defaults): install the GitHub auth provider the e2e suite signs in with\n\nThe third spec drives the session-auth API for `github`, but the backend never\nhad that provider. `/api/auth/github/start` answers 404 with\n`{\"error\":{\"name\":\"NotFoundError\",\"message\":\"Unknown auth provider ''github''\"}}`\n— which is what the popup contains when the test times out waiting for it to\nreach github.com — and the backend log confirms it, registering only\n`Configuring auth provider: oidc` and `guest`.\n\n`auth.providers.github` in app-config-rhdh.yaml only CONFIGURES a provider. The\nbackend module has to be installed as a dynamic plugin, and RHDH''s default list\ndoes not carry it: the install log shows the auth modules present are keycloak,\nguest and oidc, with no github one even in the disabled set. Per rhdh:docs/auth.md\nthe provider comes from an overlay package this repo publishes, which is what is\nadded here. It was never installed — the test and its app-config landed together\nin aaa32ef6 and the workspace has never had a dynamic-plugins.yaml — so the test\nhas been asserting a provider that was not there since it was written.\n\nThe e2e-test-utils `auth: \"github\"` preset installs the same package, but it also\nsets `signInPage: github`, which would replace the OIDC/Keycloak sign-in this\nsuite logs in with. So the module is added directly rather than by switching the\npreset.\n\nWhy the workspace''s own three packages are re-listed here: adding this file\nSUPPRESSES the auto-generation from metadata/. `_buildDynamicPluginsConfig` in\ne2e-test-utils takes the user config INSTEAD of the metadata-derived one, and\n`injectMetadataConfig` only maps over entries already present, so it never adds\nthem back. Verified against 2.1.11 rather than assumed: a file listing only the\nprovider resolves to a single-plugin deployment with all three app-defaults\npackages gone. Re-listing them is also what every other workspace carrying this\nfile already does — acr, topology, tekton, scorecard and eleven more.\n\nVerified the resulting plugin list through the package''s own\nprocessPluginsForDeployment: the three app-defaults entries come out identical to\ntoday''s auto-generated output, pluginConfig included, plus the provider with its\ncredentials intact.\n\nThis fixes one of the two failures on this PR. The other — the Catalog sidebar\nlink being unclickable because the sticky global-header covers it — is a\nseparate, layout-level problem and is not addressed here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(app-defaults): mark the Catalog click expected-to-fail on RHDHBUGS-3627\n\nThe suite''s remaining failure is not a test problem. The global header is a\nsticky MuiAppBar with z-index 1100 and the sidebar list starts at the top of the\nviewport, so its first item — Catalog — renders underneath it. Playwright\nretried the click for 10 seconds, 21 attempts, each reporting the element\nvisible, enabled, stable and scrolled into view, then blocked by\n`<nav id=\"global-header\">`. The screenshot confirms it: the first visible\nsidebar entry is Create, and Catalog is nowhere on screen while the\naccessibility tree has it as the first sidebar child. A user with a mouse cannot\nopen Catalog either.\n\nThat is RHDHBUGS-3627, which absorbed RHDHBUGS-3573 (\"Global header overlaps top\ncontent of sidebar navigation\") — the exact symptom here. The video, screenshots\nand an offline reproduction recipe are attached to that ticket. Its fix,\nredhat-developer/rhdh-plugins#4405, is still open, so no image the e2e lanes\npull carries it yet.\n\n`test.fail`, not `test.skip`, and that is the point of this commit rather than\nan implementation detail. This PR exists because a skip went stale: it cited\nRHIDP-15482, the ticket closed, nobody re-read the test, and the workspace sat\nwith no nightly coverage for months. Replacing one skip with another would\nrebuild the same debt against a different ticket.\n\n`fail` does not have that failure mode. Verified against the runner this repo\npins (@playwright/test 1.59.1) rather than assumed:\n\n  - while the bug exists: the test reports ✘ but the run is green, and the\n    other two tests keep running — so nightly coverage is restored for them.\n  - once the bug is fixed: \"Expected to fail, but passed.\" → the run goes red\n    until someone deletes the marker.\n\nCI becomes the reminder instead of a person. Applied unconditionally rather than\ngated on E2E_NIGHTLY_MODE, because the overlap breaks the PR check too.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(app-defaults): record why the expected-failure is not a flake\n\nReview feedback on #3419: the unconditional test.fail could report \"Expected to\nfail, but passed\" if the overlap turned out to depend on runner viewport or\ntiming, which would read as brittleness rather than as the reminder firing.\n\nIt does not. From the failing run''s artifacts: 23 click attempts over 10s, every\none blocked by `<nav id=\"global-header\">`, none succeeding — and reproduced at\nboth 1920x1080 (screenshot) and 1280x720 (video). The overlap is geometric.\n\nNoting it in the comment so whoever hits the red knows to look for the fix\nhaving landed rather than for a flake.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(app-defaults): use `enabled: true`, the field the install CLI asks for\n\nReview feedback on #3419. The repo is mixed — 10 of the 15 workspaces carrying a\ndynamic-plugins.yaml use `enabled`, 5 use `disabled` — but the tie-breaker is\nnot the count. `isPluginDisabled` in the install CLI treats them as equivalent\nand then says which it wants:\n\n    if (hasEnabled && hasDisabled) {\n      warn(`... specifies both ''enabled'' and ''disabled''. The ''enabled'' field\n            takes precedence; please use only ''enabled''.`);\n\nSo `enabled: true` is what the tool asks for, and following the majority happens\nto agree with it rather than the other way round.\n\nRe-ran the plugin resolution after the change: same four packages, the three\napp-defaults ones still identical to the metadata-generated output, and the\nprovider''s credentials intact.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(app-defaults): use test.skip, matching the documented convention\n\nReview feedback on #3419: `test.fail` had no prior use anywhere in the repo, and\nAGENTS.md prescribes `test.skip` for a known product bug. Switching to `skip`\nrather than introducing a second pattern by side-effect — a repo-wide convention\nis a decision for the team to take deliberately, not one a PR about an\napp-defaults skip should make on its way past.\n\nThis gives up the property `fail` had: it turned the run red with \"Expected to\nfail, but passed\" the day the bug was fixed, so CI was the reminder. A skip\ncannot do that — verified rather than assumed, the run is byte-identical whether\nthe bug is present or not.\n\nSince nothing in this repo will notice the fix landing, the reminder is split\nacross both ends and the comment says so plainly:\n\n  - here, a REMOVE THIS note naming RHDHBUGS-3627 and rhdh-plugins#4405, and\n    stating outright that no signal will arrive;\n  - on RHDHBUGS-3627, a comment pointing back at this file, so whoever closes\n    the ticket is told there is a test to unskip.\n\nThat pair is weaker than a red build and the comment does not pretend otherwise.\nIt is, at least, aimed at an OPEN ticket with a linked upstream fix, which is\nthe part the RHIDP-15482 skip got wrong: it cited a ticket that closed, and the\nstaleness went unnoticed for months.\n\nKept unconditional rather than gated on E2E_NIGHTLY_MODE, because the overlap\nbreaks the PR check too.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(app-defaults): give the skip a root-cause summary, not a bare ticket id\n\nReview feedback on #3419. AGENTS.md prescribes `test.skip(condition, \"<root\ncause summary>\")`, and the repo''s other conditional skips follow it — homepage\nwrites \"homepage-backend defaultWidgets are not supported on NFS yet\". A bare\n\"RHDHBUGS-3627\" was the only one that made a reader open Jira to learn what is\nbroken.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(app-defaults): stop duplicating the plugins the app-next layer already ships\n\nThe e2e run on 5477fc66 never reached a test. The install init container aborted\nand the pod came up Init:Error, so RHDH never started:\n\n    InstallException: Duplicate OCI plugin configuration for\n    oci://…/red-hat-developer-hub-backstage-plugin-app-auth!…\n    found at the same level in dynamic-plugins.yaml:\n    oci://…/app-auth:pr_3419__0.1.1__coverage!…\n\nMy doing. The file listed all three of the workspace''s packages on the reasoning\nthat a user config suppresses the metadata auto-generation — true — but two of\nthem were already coming from somewhere else. The new-frontend-system layer\nships app-auth and app-integrations, and it is merged in automatically because\nthis project''s namespace ends in `-app-next`.\n\nThey did not collapse into one entry because the two merge paths do not dedupe\nalike. `_mergeGeneratedWithBase` passes `normalizeKey:\ngetNormalizedPluginMergeKey`, which collapses the same plugin across differing\ntags; `_mergeBaseConfigs`, which is the path a user config takes, keys on the raw\n`package` string alone. So `app-auth:bs_1.49.4__0.0.1` from that layer and\n`app-auth:bs_1.52.0__0.1.1` from this file survived as two entries, then\n`resolvePluginPackages` rewrote both to the same pr_ ref — and the installer\nrejects that.\n\nOnly `app-defaults` and the provider are listed now. Both omissions are load\nbearing, so the file says why rather than leaving the next person to rediscover\nit by breaking the deployment again.\n\nThe earlier verification missed this because it simulated\n`processPluginsForDeployment` on the file alone — the step where the layers are\nmerged was never exercised. Redone over the full path this time, replaying\n`_mergeBaseConfigs` with the same three base layers and merge options the\ndeployment uses:\n\n  - before: 10 plugins, app-auth and app-integrations duplicated\n  - after: 8 plugins, no duplicates\n  - against main''s current behaviour: an identical 7-plugin set plus the\n    provider, which is the whole intended delta\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(app-defaults): override backstage compatibility to 1.54.4\n\n* test(app-defaults): trim the comments, drop the stale backstage pin\n\nReview findings on this branch:\n\n- The comments were 27 of 44 lines in `dynamic-plugins.yaml` — the highest\n  ratio of any e2e config in the repo — and near-verbatim copies of the\n  commit messages they came from. The rationale belongs in the commit and\n  the PR body; the file keeps the two facts a reader needs at that line.\n\n- `backstage.json` pinned 1.54.4 while `source.json` says 1.52.1 and the\n  metadata says `bs_1.52.0__`. It came from an `/override-backstage` run\n  whose metadata refresh failed, so the pin landed and nothing else did,\n  making this the only workspace whose pin is a minor off its own metadata.\n  It is not inert: `bootstrapPluginBuilds.py` only uses a workspace''s own\n  version when the workspace is flagged outdated, and that check is\n  minor-only — the pin clears the flag, so the next bootstrap would emit\n  `bs_1.54.6__` tags against e2e entries hardcoded at `bs_1.52.0__`.\n  Removing it leaves `source.json` to keep the workspace correctly flagged.\n\n- `signIn.resolvers: usernameMatchingUserEntityName` contradicted the doc\n  the comment cites: GitHub is here for the session-auth API only, Keycloak\n  owns sign-in, and the spec closes the popup at github.com without ever\n  completing the handshake. Removed, so GitHub cannot issue an identity.\n\n- `clientId`/`clientSecret` were declared in both `app-config-rhdh.yaml` and\n  the plugin''s `pluginConfig`. The provider block now lives in one file,\n  with `callbackUrl` alongside the credentials it belongs to.\n\nAlso merged main: the branch was 49 commits behind and its last green e2e\npredates two of its own commits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvSqtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2r4QAA/rCOvrWu5008+Bo7MpAnkD\nXyA00b7j/04UF53zCpYUckfFHVxk4lrt0XQLSdmE0SDd3wwH+N+mw//wOkOGlABW\niKoTdT/7UklluRbhmaLzzePtiumz+foKXcJrI1is7TB6XEY8VCmmxwWpSqUryW0G\ng6UFtllnW13bPLM8sjTdWTn3nUkjNgHuKiDAIYt93vo+YdE+NZOigl6yftGjClLH\ne/nLxewiE3wJy0N3HcHnAL7N7clIijoqmuB4cMnt1O5Zu/aQ5s0lEcjwRaR5AoTD\ncO93dWIaoYEn6HlAfaXu0BQJsyUHAkqfK1yho3UOLOmmbExLHO4d7sxAFPcjGOXH\nuoD/3aVO1gng0hdIqhNi6Yv1Q2m5LEpHJzyNKH9W7LAcoM0HKB4PtzW4iV7lvB4E\n/Vf3s4nD/SY60UcDCvy/XRnNVWIzrXe85GaCQ5LiNOR8HO5WOTh4dlM6rHTnpQwH\nV0pPMc1aOpkKYkfYAzxR5/bUo2g+io1uflx3P+pEgATCaAnBttgO0GwuvKyMaoz/\nMGXTVn1VU9Oh0t+r0Xv2MLzeXbZaIhH0SrPOQc7gyQXMZ0n18vs1SE3DR1B77YD3\nQCit1uUYbroo2mHA1Co7i5XNz9HOCZ2qla81NCoraxs+ouZPLz/QMN59AuJzpG6x\nVbMyaQ9R3/9ayLuKaCX7\n=FEfQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T15:28:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redhat-developer/rhdh-plugin-export-overlays/commit/bae3d55ceebef157c3ddadd6f3dfa3aa55c6c9d3","node_id":"C_kwDONrRnPNoAKGJhZTNkNTVjZWViZWYxNTdjM2RkYWRkNmYzZGZhM2FhNTVjNmM5ZDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redhat-developer/rhdh-plugin-export-overlays/commit/646d983f0a6b3ae10061046e540ecf058d23de3c","sha":"646d983f0a6b3ae10061046e540ecf058d23de3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-plugin-export-overlays/commits/646d983f0a6b3ae10061046e540ecf058d23de3c"}],"sha":"bae3d55ceebef157c3ddadd6f3dfa3aa55c6c9d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-plugin-export-overlays/commits/bae3d55ceebef157c3ddadd6f3dfa3aa55c6c9d3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1463004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gustavolira","id":1463004,"login":"gustavolira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NjMwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-plugin-export-overlays/commits/646d983f0a6b3ae10061046e540ecf058d23de3c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T14:27:51Z","email":"guga.java@gmail.com","name":"Gustavo Lira e Silva"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T14:27:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(smoke): replicate the RHDH backend loader behaviour plugins rely on (#4002)\n\n* fix(smoke): replicate the RHDH backend loader behaviour plugins rely on\n\nThe native smoke harness reported load and boot failures that RHDH itself\ndoes not have. They kept the nightly plugin sweep and the catalog index\nsanity run red and hid the real artifact defects (RHIDP-17310):\n\n- resolvePackagePath() requires `<pkg>/package.json` by the non-dynamic\n  name. RHDH''s CommonJSModuleLoader redirects that request to the installed\n  `<pkg>-dynamic` plugin; the harness now does the same. Every plugin with\n  a database failed to load without it (corrects RHDHBUGS-3557).\n- Modules whose host plugin nothing in the run provides get a static copy\n  of it for auth, events and notifications, which RHDH ships statically.\n- core.dynamicplugins gets an empty implementation, which the extensions\n  plugins need to start.\n- Dependency-free feature loaders are expanded before boot, including the\n  CJS module.exports an import() yields. startTestBackend adds a\n  placeholder plugin for every module whose plugin it cannot see, so\n  scorecard-backend (a loader) collided with it.\n- In a --support run, an out-of-scope backend plugin `<x>` is installed\n  when an in-scope module is named `<x>-module-*`, so scorecard''s\n  dev-preview modules boot with their tech-preview host.\n- Dummy config for tech-radar, apiconnect, dynatrace-dql,\n  github-discussions, notifications email and scorecard jira, plus\n  backend.database, which RHDH always sets.\n\nIt also stops failing every CLI 2.1 artifact on the frontend config-key\ncross-check (RHIDP-17311). Those exports ship module federation only, and\nmain''s NFS app no longer reads `dynamicPlugins.frontend`. Keys that belong\nto an MF-only bundle are reported in `frontend.configKeysNotApplicable`\ninstead of as mismatches.\n\nAgainst the published artifacts, 22 of the 24 workspace/tier runs that\nfailed now pass. The other two are the real metadata defects in\nRHDHBUGS-3837.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(smoke): harden loader parity from the deep review\n\nCorrectness:\n- expandFeatureLoaders keeps service factories a loader yields apart and\n  startBackend hands them back inside a dependency-free loader. Flattened in,\n  a factory for a service already provided became an explicit duplicate\n  (\"Duplicate service implementations\"), where the backend skips it for a\n  loader.\n- A loader that throws is reported with its description, as the backend''s\n  ForwardedError does, instead of a bare error with no plugin attached.\n- backendStart.hostPlugins is reported on a failed boot too; it was dropped\n  exactly when an injected host could be the cause.\n- Cross-tier hosts are chosen from the modules actually installed, not every\n  in-scope package: an excluded or non-OCI module no longer pulls in a host.\n- HOST_FALLBACKS is a Map; `id in` on an object literal also matched\n  prototype keys.\n- MF-only frontend plugins are matched to their bundles by name rather than\n  by array index.\n\nDocs and comments:\n- Hosts from another tier are loaded and booted in this run, so a defect in\n  one fails it too; report.ts, README and a test comment said otherwise.\n- backend.database: startTestBackend''s database service does read it (the\n  value equals its fallback); the comment said it was ignored.\n- \"the four below\" listed six dummy configs; named loader nesting cap.\n\nTests (each seen failing against a mutation first): the Module._resolveFilename\npatch itself (now returns an unpatch), declaredScalprumName, nested loaders,\nloader service factories, loader error attribution, excluded module pulls\nno host. harness-logic.test.ts imports moved to the top, no dynamic imports.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(smoke): say why backend-dynamic-feature-service is a real dependency\n\nA review suggested replacing it with a locally declared core.dynamicplugins\nref. That lets the extensions plugins start, but they require() the\npackage itself at load time, so the swap turns extensions tech-preview\nfrom pass (2/2) back into fail-load (0/2). Recorded next to the import so\nthe suggestion is not repeated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(smoke): align loader-parity code with the catalog-index probe paths\n\nSecond deep-review pass, after the rebase onto #3991.\n\n- Error reports keep `workspace` as well as `catalogIndex`. Workspace mode\n  does not probe refs, so an out-of-tier host the install CLI refuses aborts\n  the whole install; the status: error report dropped `workspace.hosts` and\n  gave no hint that an out-of-tier ref was involved. Verified with a forced\n  install failure on scorecard [dev-preview]: `workspace` was absent before,\n  present with `hosts` after.\n- The loader that carries expandFeatureLoaders'' service factories now runs\n  before every loader kept in the feature list (bootFeatureList). The\n  backend runs loaders in order, and a loader depending on a root service\n  one of those factories provides failed with \"No service available\" when\n  it ran first, a failure RHDH does not have.\n- unwrapDefault takes off one level, as the backend''s unwrapFeature does,\n  instead of recursing without bound. Deeper nesting now fails here as it\n  does in RHDH.\n- An install exclusion that removes a module''s cross-tier host is recorded\n  in `exclusions` and logged, like every other install exclusion. Before,\n  the module failed to boot with nothing in the report saying why.\n- WorkspaceInfo.outOfScope doc: hosts are counted there and are validated.\n- README: the static notifications host brings plugin-notifications-node\n  and -common into the harness''s node_modules, which RHDH does not ship, so\n  an export that fails to embed them no longer fails here.\n\nEach new test was seen failing against the old behaviour.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(smoke): clear the SonarCloud findings on the loader-parity code\n\n- main() cognitive complexity back under 15 (S3776): the frontend\n  config-key cross-check, with its MF-only set-aside and its logging, moves\n  to checkFrontendConfigKeys(). Behaviour is unchanged: results.json is\n  byte-identical before and after for scorecard [tech-preview],\n  adoption-insights [generally-available] and backstage [tech-preview],\n  all three of which exercise configKeysNotApplicable, and catalog-index\n  mode still omits both fields.\n- expandFeatureLoaders walks the list recursively instead of awaiting in a\n  loop (S9382, both awaits), as partitionResolvable does. Kept sequential\n  rather than Promise.all: the backend runs loaders one at a time in list\n  order, and running them concurrently would reorder side effects of\n  loaders that are not independent.\n- Optional chains in featureTargets and unwrapDefault (S6582).\n- A loader description is used only when it is a string (S6551).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(smoke): assert the dependent loader receives the loader-provided service\n\nSonar flagged the bootFeatureList test as having no assertion\n(typescript:S2699): it relied on startTestBackend not throwing. It now\nrecords the service the dependent loader is handed and asserts it. It\nfails when bootFeatureList stops registering loader services first.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b79dbf971d80f032bab2e392931f0180abd36402","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-plugin-export-overlays/git/trees/b79dbf971d80f032bab2e392931f0180abd36402"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-plugin-export-overlays/git/commits/646d983f0a6b3ae10061046e540ecf058d23de3c","verification":{"payload":"tree b79dbf971d80f032bab2e392931f0180abd36402\nparent 7aa4203addfc361f11c6a177e15b32a8750e75af\nauthor Gustavo 