nd-dynamic-feature-service is a real dependency\n\nA review suggested replacing it with a locally declared core.dynamicplugins\nref. That lets the extensions plugins start, but they require() the\npackage itself at load time, so the swap turns extensions tech-preview\nfrom pass (2/2) back into fail-load (0/2). Recorded next to the import so\nthe suggestion is not repeated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(smoke): align loader-parity code with the catalog-index probe paths\n\nSecond deep-review pass, after the rebase onto #3991.\n\n- Error reports keep `workspace` as well as `catalogIndex`. Workspace mode\n  does not probe refs, so an out-of-tier host the install CLI refuses aborts\n  the whole install; the status: error report dropped `workspace.hosts` and\n  gave no hint that an out-of-tier ref was involved. Verified with a forced\n  install failure on scorecard [dev-preview]: `workspace` was absent before,\n  present with `hosts` after.\n- The loader that carries expandFeatureLoaders'' service factories now runs\n  before every loader kept in the feature list (bootFeatureList). The\n  backend runs loaders in order, and a loader depending on a root service\n  one of those factories provides failed with \"No service available\" when\n  it ran first, a failure RHDH does not have.\n- unwrapDefault takes off one level, as the backend''s unwrapFeature does,\n  instead of recursing without bound. Deeper nesting now fails here as it\n  does in RHDH.\n- An install exclusion that removes a module''s cross-tier host is recorded\n  in `exclusions` and logged, like every other install exclusion. Before,\n  the module failed to boot with nothing in the report saying why.\n- WorkspaceInfo.outOfScope doc: hosts are counted there and are validated.\n- README: the static notifications host brings plugin-notifications-node\n  and -common into the harness''s node_modules, which RHDH does not ship, so\n  an export that fails to embed them no longer fails here.\n\nEach new test was seen failing against the old behaviour.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(smoke): clear the SonarCloud findings on the loader-parity code\n\n- main() cognitive complexity back under 15 (S3776): the frontend\n  config-key cross-check, with its MF-only set-aside and its logging, moves\n  to checkFrontendConfigKeys(). Behaviour is unchanged: results.json is\n  byte-identical before and after for scorecard [tech-preview],\n  adoption-insights [generally-available] and backstage [tech-preview],\n  all three of which exercise configKeysNotApplicable, and catalog-index\n  mode still omits both fields.\n- expandFeatureLoaders walks the list recursively instead of awaiting in a\n  loop (S9382, both awaits), as partitionResolvable does. Kept sequential\n  rather than Promise.all: the backend runs loaders one at a time in list\n  order, and running them concurrently would reorder side effects of\n  loaders that are not independent.\n- Optional chains in featureTargets and unwrapDefault (S6582).\n- A loader description is used only when it is a string (S6551).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(smoke): assert the dependent loader receives the loader-provided service\n\nSonar flagged the bootFeatureList test as having no assertion\n(typescript:S2699): it relied on startTestBackend not throwing. It now\nrecords the service the dependent loader is handed and asserts it. It\nfails when bootFeatureList stops registering loader services first.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvRxnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8dQQAKAh0VI5LUsb1ZFc5fibTaWp\nJ7ckPBTfkU/x8+ItoYLXTEKofBa1nB0MEFY8V0jAo6RLloUskPfkhb1VTkdk5vgF\n9ofnKFBpBA8vNuHvYIynqT2sR1TLSgjVysKwRDurEXCC3G001Y2F3gX2UrC1q0Vg\nbzGyUy8PZ2dJozJNxpWMHKQX+hlOmVaz055gfJDxeF08DaJyuupI