,{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1463004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gustavolira","id":1463004,"login":"gustavolira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NjMwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-plugin-export-overlays/commits/985ae7df817ca17284c2845564c068e1b663e88b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T12:48:24Z","email":"guga.java@gmail.com","name":"Gustavo Lira e Silva"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T12:48:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(smoke): stop one broken catalog index ref from aborting the whole sanity run (#3991)\n\n* fix(smoke): stop one broken catalog index ref from aborting the whole sanity run\n\nThe nightly catalog-index-sanity run has been red every day since it was\nadded, and for most of that time it validated nothing: the install CLI\ntreats the config as one unit, so a single ref it refuses aborts the\ninstall and the run reports 0/0 loaded. The `next` index carried such a\nref throughout, a different one each week (unpublished `2.0.0--`/`2.1.0--`\ntags for keycloak-provider, scorecard-dependabot and now\nbackstage-plugin-org).\n\nCatalog-index mode now probes every ref before installing, doing what the\nCLI does first: `skopeo inspect --raw`, plus the plugin-path auto-detection\ncheck on the `io.backstage.dynamic-packages` annotation. Refs it would\nrefuse are left out, recorded in `catalogIndex.unresolved` (report schema\n10), and fail the run as `fail-install`. Everything else is still\ninstalled, loaded and booted. The job summary and the triage issue name\neach refused ref first.\n\nAgainst today''s `next` index this goes from 0 validated packages to 59 of\n69. It also shows that the index has 10 uninstallable refs, not just the\norg one: nine 2.1 scorecard images ship an empty annotation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(smoke): move install gating and fail-install check out of main()\n\nSonar S3776 flagged main() at cognitive complexity 16 after the\nunresolved-ref handling landed there. The two decisions it added, skipping\nthe install when nothing is left and failing the install on unresolved\nrefs, move into installSource() and installFailed(). No behaviour change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(smoke): probe the quay fallback the install CLI uses for productized refs\n\nThe install CLI resolves an image under registry.access.redhat.com/rhdh/ that is not\nthere yet to quay.io/rhdh/ (resolveImage in cli-module-install-dynamic-plugins). The\nprobe only asked the named registry, so against an RC index, whose refs point at\nimages not yet released, it would have left out packages the CLI installs fine.\nprobeCandidates() returns the images in the CLI''s order and probeRegistry() tries\neach; the fallback image is named in the error only when both were tried.\n\nAlso reflow the sanity step comment, move the unresolved-refs jq line above the\n`.plugin` comment that belongs to the next command, and say that installSource()\nskips an empty config in every mode, not only catalog-index.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(smoke): make probe failures say what happened, and keep them on a crash\n\nReview findings on the catalog-index probe:\n\n- A missing skopeo binary was recorded against every ref, so the report blamed ~70\n  packages for a tool problem. ENOENT now fails the run with that cause.\n- A probe killed by its timeout recorded \"Command failed: skopeo ...\", never saying it\n  timed out. It now records \"no answer within 30s\". The timeout drops from 60s to 30s:\n  it multiplies by 2 candidates x 3 attempts per ref during an outage, and the job''s\n  60-minute limit cancels the run instead of failing it.\n- With the quay fallback, a double failure kept only quay''s error. Both are kept.\n- writeErrorReport dropped the catalogIndex block, so a crash after the probe (the CLI\n  failing on a ref the probe let through) lost the refused refs from the job summary\n  and the triage issue, the two places that list them first.\n- lastErrorLine moves to util.ts next to errorMessage, uses isRecord instead of a\n  cast, and gets a test. pluginPathProblem uses errorMessage and isRecord instead of\n  repeating them, and imageNameFromRef reuses registryRefFromOciRef.\n- The workflow summary falls back to \"?\" for a missing ref or error, like the line\n  after it. The README names the third refusal reason (several plugins, no selector),\n  the attempt count and the registry fallback.\n- A renderer test covers a malformed unresolved list.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(smoke): move probe error classification out of probeRegistry\n\nSonar S3776 flagged probeRegistry at cognitive complexity 16 after the ENOENT and\ntimeout handling landed in its catch block. probeErrorLine() now owns turning one\nskopeo failure into a report line (or throwing for a missing skopeo), and\nprobeRegistry keeps only the candidate loop.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(smoke): retry and drain the probe queue recursively\n\nSonar flagged the three awaits inside loops in partitionResolvable\n(typescript:S9382). All three are sequential on purpose: a retry waits for\nthe attempt before it, and a worker takes one ref at a time. Recursion says\nthat directly. Behaviour is unchanged, and the existing tests pin it:\nattempt count, no retry on a definitive answer, the concurrency cap, and\ninput order.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"def2a9b8b2f2298f849044cdaf389cba9eb92b5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-plugin-export-overlays/git/trees/def2a9b8b2f2298f849044cdaf389cba9eb92b5f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-plugin-export-overlays/git/commits/985ae7df817ca17284c2845564c068e1b663e88b","verification":{"payload":"tree def2a9b8b2f2298f849044cdaf389cba9eb92b5f\nparent f7c85e5b9990f9a3cc86df805a50e3546b1282f8\nauthor Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com> 1790772504 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790772504 -0300\n\nfix(smoke): stop one broken catalog index ref from aborting the whole sanity run (#3991)\n\n* fix(smoke): stop one broken catalog index ref from aborting the whole sanity run\n\nThe nightly catalog-index-sanity run has been red every day since it was\nadded, and for most of that time it validated nothing: the install CLI\ntreats the config as one unit, so a single ref it refuses aborts the\ninstall and the run reports 0/0 loaded. The `next` index carried such a\nref throughout, a different one each week (unpublished `2.0.0--`/`2.1.0--`\ntags for keycloak-provider, scorecard-dependabot and now\nbackstage-plugin-org).\n\nCatalog-index mode now probes every ref before installing, doing what the\nCLI does first: `skopeo inspect --raw`, plus the plugin-path auto-detection\ncheck on the `io.backstage.dynamic-packages` annotation. Refs it would\nrefuse are left out, recorded in `catalogIndex.unresolved` (report schema\n10), and fail the run as `fail-install`. Everything else is still\ninstalled, loaded and booted. The job summary and the triage issue name\neach refused ref first.\n\nAgainst today''s `next` index this goes from 0 validated packages to 59 of\n69. It also shows that the index has 10 uninstallable refs, not just the\norg one: nine 2.1 scorecard images ship an empty annotation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(smoke): move install gating and fail-install check out of main()\n\nSonar S3776 flagged main() at cognitive complexity 16 after the\nunresolved-ref handling landed there. The two decisions it added, skipping\nthe install when nothing is left and failing the install on unresolved\nrefs, move into installSource() and installFailed(). No behaviour change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(smoke): probe the quay fallback the install CLI uses for productized refs\n\nThe install CLI resolves an image under registry.access.redhat.com/rhdh/ that is not\nthere yet to quay.io/rhdh/ (resolveImage in cli-module-install-dynamic-plugins). The\nprobe only asked the named registry, so against an RC index, whose refs point at\nimages not yet released, it would have left out packages the CLI installs fine.\nprobeCandidates() returns the images in the CLI''s order and probeRegistry() tries\neach; the fallback image is named in the error only when both were tried.\n\nAlso reflow the sanity step comment, move the unresolved-refs jq line above the\n`.plugin` comment that belongs to the next command, and say that installSource()\nskips an empty config in every mode, not only catalog-index.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(smoke): make probe failures say what happened, and keep them on a crash\n\nReview findings on the catalog-index probe:\n\n- A missing skopeo binary was recorded against every ref, so the report blamed ~70\n  packages for a tool problem. ENOENT now fails the run with that cause.\n- A probe killed by its timeout recorded \"Command failed: skopeo ...\", never saying it\n  timed out. It now records \"no answer within 30s\". The timeout drops from 60s to 30s:\n  it multiplies by 2 candidates x 3 attempts per ref during an outage, and the job''s\n  60-minute limit cancels the run instead of failing it.\n- With the quay fallback, a double failure kept only quay''s error. Both are kept.\n- writeErrorReport dropped the catalogIndex block, so a crash after the probe (the CLI\n  failing on a ref the probe let through) lost the refused refs from the job summary\n  and the triage issue, the two places that list them first.\n- lastErrorLine moves to util.ts next to errorMessage, uses isRecord instead of a\n  cast, and gets a test. pluginPathProblem uses errorMessage and isRecord instead of\n  repeating them, and imageNameFromRef reuses registryRefFromOciRef.\n- The workflow summary falls back to \"?\" for a missing ref or error, like the line\n  after it. The README names the third refusal reason (several plugins, no selector),\n  the attempt count and the registry fallback.\n- A renderer test covers a malformed unresolved list.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(smoke): move probe error classification out of probeRegistry\n\nSonar S3776 flagged probeRegistry at cognitive complexity 16 after the ENOENT and\ntimeout handling landed in its catch block. probeErrorLine() now owns turning one\nskopeo failure into a report line (or throwing for a missing skopeo), and\nprobeRegistry keeps only the candidate loop.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(smoke): retry and drain the probe queue recursively\n\nSonar flagged the three awaits inside loops in partitionResolvable\n(typescript:S9382). All three are sequential on purpose: a retry waits for\nthe attempt before it, and a worker takes one ref at a time. Recursion says\nthat directly. Behaviour is unchanged, and the existing tests pin it:\nattempt count, no retry on a definitive answer, the concurrency cap, and\ninput order.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvQUYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnvkQAEw5/9FUkqdeaKJlMtAWxv+u\nbs0JY6PFHclkoHx9svmqqQttIO0m0xiUaWErYfAFTM736X3jJMhJCMH4WLIHi/wb\nMubee3MA6qvmR9J2MA1bMOBxZ9LtsTkIfQgtjmryMvwzyabPrKv0xxpiaD+HktO8\noKZqLfpQvQ3senUn83wwywrvZ1nq9IW8FplDoN6OCaTdH+I32M/iBevL7suLz+Mt\n9mK3tSjczLGUOpr6qaJgDDRjlgGLVDf5y5mOB/USQh4CYJRoJQqN+pkil2t0Lwsx\n5obKxDeIXkd7mrdviK/6kq7aot/P6+STjiAveYJQED2+9mDh6fcfnaaLR8Ppbpw6\nc8pLNPG1EmM/LJK0DavYZl9H8OV7fKY7yhYOiulncQ9tCe4pzJ0HLgCcRfjB/Ytv\ndUZyr0VtIwBBsnP67xwrJYIYWEcBEv178HMPWVkVJZ7e5K435uScDfFV8AFe28Jk\nRknFADnLCW+LrL+aPiW2v8oXhkG1m1bLGwi+3pzygG0akqNoaJPsRdOCdqXAdT4K\naZSsMbrCOw4u2UenxZVGDwuc3tPly5sGOl6jjE/Dky0mz8XMylvmBc+Pz00SYHoT\nhISjRKGxhpDZIFfGVGnfENztZicjj6kd1wSCayj5f/ENXgbXbmk490DywRnzLeI8\nZJuS721dB6lSXTPTjDr5\n=Sqmi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T12:48:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/use