users/jacobdewar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jacobdewar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aaronshaf/canvas-lms/commits/8f0186ac19b0c7420237087c6a2bef6b633f3d23/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-23T18:31:06Z","email":"jacob.dewar@instructure.com","name":"Jacob DeWar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-23T19:46:55Z","email":"jacob.dewar@instructure.com","name":"Jacob DeWar"},"message":"Convert pseudonyms spec to request spec\n\nRewrite the password/forgot/set_password/create/\nupdate/destroy/sharding groups to type: :request\nwith URL-based calls. assigns/render_template checks\nbecome response- and DB-state assertions (e.g. a\nreset is proven by the cc''s confirmation_code\nchanging). before(:once) becomes before(:each) to\navoid shared in-memory object flake.\n\nThe elevated-auth and site-admin-restriction groups\nstay controller specs in a second describe block:\nthey drive the login-management auth gate via\ninjected internals (AccessTokenAttributes,\nPseudonymAttributes, @real_current_user) that don''t\nsurvive the real request middleware, so converting\nthem makes allowed cases fail and blocked cases pass\nvacuously. A few service-boundary stubs (LoadAccount,\nsharding lookups) are also kept as-is.\n\nrefs QE-124\nflag=none\n\ntest plan:\n- bin/rspec spec/controllers/pseudonyms_controller_spec.rb\n- verify 107 examples pass\n- verify request groups use type: :request + literal URLs\n\nChange-Id: Ie83000f505ef8f495e86080ed69e6c9d900b2461\nReviewed-on: https://gerrit.instructure.com/c/canvas-lms/+/414822\nTested-by: Service Cloud Jenkins <svc.cloudjenkins@instructure.com>\nReviewed-by: Danail Kozhuharov <danail.kozhuharov@instructure.com>\nQA-Review: Jacob DeWar <jacob.dewar@instructure.com>\nProduct-Review: Jacob DeWar <jacob.dewar@instructure.com>","tree":{"sha":"48a426a5e8848d4bbb9e0de8f7c60cae2a127295","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aaronshaf/canvas-lms/gi